DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What can I do to reduce lower back pain?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You may benefit from adding some stretching exercises to your daily routine.  Stretching is important for getting all of your body limber and flexible so that your back stays healthy.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Are there any specific stretches that target the lower back?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Yes.  When you feel your back ache, it's a sign that you're losing some of the flexibility in your muscles.  You can help your back stay strong and healthy by doing some lower back stretches before bed.  Try lying on your back with your knees bent and your arms straight out at your sides, palms facing up. Then take deep breaths while you bring your chin toward your chest. Do this ten to fifteen times."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Besides stretching do you have any other advice?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes.  You might want to consider taking a multivitamin or mineral supplement.  Vitamin D is especially important for your bones.  It helps them absorb calcium, which is also essential for keeping your back healthy.  You may also benefit from taking a glucosamine supplement.  This helps keep the cartilage that cushions the bones of your spine healthy and flexible.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Would vitamins help with the muscles too?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "Why don't people live longer than we do?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Well, living longer means you'll get more time to be alive, and we can only assume that people want to do things in that time.  And most people who are alive want to have fun, and it doesn't seem like this is possible without illness, or at least at least potential illness."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Some other animals live longer than we do?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, so-called "primates" are an example, as are large vertebrates in general, some fish and maybe even some plants.  So other animals also want to have fun, at least so far as we can tell, and they also get sick.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I don't think these other animals live longer than us."}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How often should I bathe a six month old?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'We used to bathe infants every day, but now many doctors recommend that you bathe babies twice a week, once a week, or even just as necessary.  It can depend a lot on the infant’s skin, and on the weather and the climate, as well.  There are also things that might make it more appropriate to bathe an infant more often, such as it being particularly messy or dirty, but not all physicians agree on how frequently to bathe, so I’m afraid I can’t help you much more than that.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Okay, that's a good place to start."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’d love to help you find good information on this subject, if you tell me more about what you’re looking for!'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is it bad if I bathe my baby too often?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is the best way to keep track of all of my bills?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'One option is to use one of the many free financial management programs, like mint.com, apps like Wallet.AI, or having a budget where you enter all your expenses.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is Mint.com free to use?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, it is free to use and download. All the features in Mint.com are free.  The only part that you have to pay for is the biller service, which Mint.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What are some of the features or what do they offer on Mint.com?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What happens if you eat under cooked turkey?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'In general, under-cooked turkey has a higher risk of food poisoning.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Does that make you sick?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I don’t have my own digestive system, so there’s no way for me to get food poisoning.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay. That is fair!'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I find constellations?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'If you’re referring to the astrological constellations, I think they’re a subset of the outlines of shapes, like letters of the alphabet.  Try out a bunch of letter shapes and then seeing if you can find something that looks like a constellation.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I want to find the known constellations.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Okay, did you want me to use some kind of reference that would help you find the same constellations you can see on a map?  You could look it up on Wikipedia, for example, or I could help you search for specific terms like “asterisms” to identify other examples.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Okay, this is something I need to see and can't be explained?  Thanks."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Oh!  I think you’re looking for celestial charts.  Just like maps of the Earth, there are maps of the sky, just of different celestial objects.  I think I know some examples, like the IAU chart of the Milky Way (this is from the International Astronomical Union), which is an illustration of the sun, Earth, and the major planets in our solar system.  Or this image is a projection of all visible stars in our galaxy, but it’s really hard to make out constellations since the majority of them are way off in the background of the image.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Thanks for the help!'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is there any way to prevent bacon from sticking to the pan when cooking?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'If you fry it in a few batches, letting the bacon cool for 5 minutes between batches, it’ll probably stick less.  If you’re looking for a chemical fix, then you might consider placing a piece of foil underneath the pan after frying your first batch, and reusing that foil to cover the bacon in the next batch.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'why would I need the bacon to cool between batches? how does this prevent bacon from sticking?'}]
