DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'My waterproof jacket shell keeps wetting out. Is this normal?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’m not really sure what you mean by “waterproof”, but you can try something called “breathability”. This will let water vapor move through your clothing, and avoid that uncomfortable trapped-sweat feeling you mention. I don’t have any precise advice for you about your particular jacket, but there are many things you could try that will get you someplace similar. Some simple things you could try would be: moving your jacket from a darker color fabric to one that’s a more natural-looking gray or off-white, or reducing the amount of thick synthetic insulation in your jacket, or layering a thin synthetic jacket over a thicker jacket. I think you might find this fabric-color chart helpful in general. You could also ask your jacket’s manufacturer or an expert, although I don’t want you to be discouraged if it’s not a simple solution.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Wetting out is actually due in part to that layered construction. The breathability of waterproof gear contributes to wetting out because when the outer layer gets wet, it increases humidity on the layer closest to your body, and then you're damp."}]
