DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "What's the best career path for someone with the INFP personality type?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The INFP personality type is one that will probably fit well in the health field, since it’s somewhat of a dual type. INFPs have relatively well-developed intuitions and are prone to sympathy, but have a somewhat weak sense of self, since they’re very driven by their emotions.  I’d also recommend going into therapy.  After all, an INFP’s most well-developed attribute is their emotional empathy, and that can be used to help others.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, so therapy, or counselling could be a good option?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'If you wanted to pursue that, yes.  There are many different kinds of therapy, and as an INFP, I think you could also consider doing a type of creative expression, like writing or painting.   But if you’re worried about practical questions, remember that there are all sorts of types of jobs that are related to counseling or therapy.  You could also consider medicine, since INFPs are so well-versed in empathy and also other emotional attributes.  Do you have other questions, or should we discuss any other careers?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay. Well, I am also interested in creative expression.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Then the best thing to do is to follow your passions.  If you’re interested in pursuing art, or writing, then go for it.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay thanks. Do I need to attend university to pursue art or writing?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I'm travelling to Moscow. Can you tell me some of the popular tourist attractions in the city?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Hey, how are you?  I think I heard you were going to Russia. Is that right? That’s exciting!  Well, there are a lot of great tourist attractions in Moscow. Let’s see, I could tell you about the Kremlin and the Cathedral of Christ the Savior, the famous Bolshoi Theatre and the Moscow Art Theatre, which is one of the world’s best. Then there’s the Red Square and the famous St. Basil’s Cathedral, which is the largest and most spectacular cathedral in Russia. It’s really beautiful. And there are many other great sights in Moscow. It’s a really great city for tourists.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Great! What kind of food and drinks are popular in Moscow?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You can try lots of delicious local Russian dishes like beef Stroganoff and Pelmeni. If you like ice cream, you should try some traditional Russian desserts like Saltykvarelo and Poppy Seed Cake.  And they also have nice cocktails, like Bitter Lemon, Wodka Daiquiri and Oreolnaya.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Thanks! Is Moscow safe for tourists?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'There’s a lot of good food and drinks, and many popular tourist attractions, but you’d probably better avoid some of the most unsafe neighborhoods.  So you should go to the tourist attractions and do other things that the police recommend.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Any other tips for visiting Moscow?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you give me a recipe for fried chicken?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sure, I can use the built-in cooking app.  We should start by measuring out some chicken pieces and frying them in oil.  The oil should be about three inches deep, and the chicken should be small enough to fit comfortably.  When the oil is hot enough, drop the chicken in and give it a nice even fry, taking care not to crowd the pan.  It’s OK to leave it in there for as long as ten minutes, but no more than 20.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What kind of oil is best to use?'}]
