DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Who was Alfred Joseph Hitchcock?  Why was he so famous?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Alfred Hitchcock was a film director who created many masterpieces such as “Rear Window” (1954) and “Psycho” (1960). He was a visionary and has impacted the way we view filmmaking as an artform.  Perhaps his most famous quote is, “The horror, the horror” and he was responsible for countless film trilogies like “Psycho”, “Vertigo”, and “The Birds”.  He also made over 50 movies that each earned him a Golden Globe Award.  He was also a very religious and creative person.  He was a Catholic, and even designed and sculpted his own church.  He also helped a friend that was becoming a nun and spent a lot of time teaching her.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Was he a film maker or a writer?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'He was both a film maker and writer.  He also directed and co-wrote many of his movies.  But he spent most of his time writing screenplays.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Where was he born?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Alfred Joseph Hitchcock was born in London, England.  He grew up in a family that loved film.  His father was a tax inspector and his mother loved films and had a theater in their home.  His siblings all became filmmakers as well.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is there a documentary about Alfred Hitchcock?'}]
