DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I teach a child sign language?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Is this an urgent request?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Yeah I think so'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'We need to look at the first level of its cognition.  I can tell that you want to use sign language, but it seems likely that this might not work for some reason.  Can I help you to set expectations?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'ok sure'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sign language is an extremely good way to communicate with people who can’t hear, but there are some caveats.  For instance, people who can see typically can communicate with others using their eyes, so they might be able to see that you’re using sign language and ignore it.  It also takes time to learn to understand a language with signs, and there are different kinds of sign languages.  That said, sign language can be very good for communication, and it’s generally better than writing or speaking.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I just want to know tips for teaching a child.'}]
