DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I stop eyeliner from smudging?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sure!  Just dab a small dot of cleanser on the end of your eyeliner, then rub your finger across the edge of the eyeliner and you should be good to go!'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I don't want to clean it off, I want to stop it from running."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "I'm sorry, I think I misunderstood what you wanted.  Are you saying you want to avoid running eyeliner?"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Yes.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sorry, I\'m afraid I\'m not an expert on makeup.  But I\'m not even sure what you\'re asking for, what do you mean by "running eyeliner"?  Are you saying your eyeliner is running, in the sense that it\'s leaving a trail?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Yeah, sort of like that.  It smudges and runs.  Do you know how to prevent that?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Ah, okay, that makes sense.  I think you can avoid that by taking extra care when applying your eyeliner.  When you're applying it, just keep the end of the eyeliner in the exact place where you want it, and hold it against the skin a bit as you make sure it goes as far as you want it to.  Do you think that will work?"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Thanks.  I will try that.'}]
