DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I'm gonna make spicy curry but I'm gonna add eggs to it, specifically hard boiled eggs. Can you tell me how to boil eggs?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Sure! To boil an egg, you first fill a pot with water, then bring it to a boil, then add the egg, and after it boils, you remove the egg from the water. It's really simple!"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What temperature should I be boiling them in?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Well, the safe temperature to boil an egg is no higher than 160o F.  Of course, you can't really control the temperature when you are using water to boil, because the temperature is different in different parts of the pot.  So if the water is at 180o F when you put the egg in, and it boils, then the temperature of the water is around 160o F right around where you are putting the egg in.  If the water is only at 140o F, then the egg will be at 160o F when you put it in."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Hmm, I dont think thats right. Im looking it up and it says to boil them in cold water'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Well, here's some clarification: You have to use cold water to drop the temperature of the egg low enough to kill any dangerous bacteria.  If you boiled the egg in normal tap water, then it wouldn't be safe.  It would be safe to use boiling water for boiling, as it is already cold.  However, I'm not a doctor, and if you want to be sure that you are doing this safely, you should ask a doctor, or just not eat it, because it's much safer not to eat an egg that is not completely cooked."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Sorry, what I meant was the eggs go in cold water but yes, you obviously boil them in high heat'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'So you are just planning to boil the egg without boiling the water?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "No, no. That's not what I said."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'OK, great! I just want to be sure that you are cooking the egg properly. You should still boil the egg in the water for several minutes, with some salt, to make sure the egg is cooked through.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, thanks'}]
