DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I make pretzels?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Well, the first thing you want to do is put a large bowl of hot water on the stove and mix in a handful of salt.  Next you want to take a slice of dough and flatten it out until it's a bit longer than your fist, then roll it out to make a rope.  You'll need to make each strand a little longer than the previous one."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Oh, how do I make the dough?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "You can use flour, water, and salt.  I would probably start by mixing together two parts water to one part flour, and a pinch of salt, then kneading it until it's smooth.  For larger pretzels I'd recommend using cold water, and possibly also freezing the flour beforehand.  You can then form it into a ball and flatten it, then keep rolling it out until you're satisfied."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'All right, do I then put it in the hot water?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "That's right.  Just drop the dough into the water and let it cook for a minute or two, then turn it over and let it cook on the other side.  You can then lift it out and set it aside to cool."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, and then what?'}]
