DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is the best way to learn a new language?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'There are a lot of different ways to learn a language, and it really depends on what you’re most interested in and what you’re trying to accomplish. You could try reading a text, like a story or novel, but you’d need to be able to read that story in your target language. You could use audio and video resources, or you could use an app to try to teach you the language.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is the best app that can teach you to speak a language without learning how to read it.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Well, a lot of apps for this kind of thing are available. One of the best ones is called "Duolingo", which you can learn more about here: https://www.duolingo.com/en-us/  It’s used by tens of millions of people around the world, and is a lot of fun. It can help you build a list of phrases and vocabulary to use while you’re learning how to speak the language. You can also practice conversations using audio recordings.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "But doesn't Duolingo require that you learn how to read the language too?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Well it’s a little tricky, but the developers of the app have actually figured out how to do it.  They’ve built an app that reads text in the language you’re learning, so it’ll be really useful for you when you’re just starting to learn the language, or if you need to learn it for work.  Also, Duolingo has built a network of users who are all learning the same language as you, so you’ll be able to exchange text with other users to get practice with real conversations.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I think you're wrong. You do have to learn how to read the language when using Duolingo."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "I think I need to apologize.  It looks like you're right, and I've made a mistake.  I should've tried to make sure that I understood the Duolingo application properly.  I’m sorry, and I want to make sure you know that I really enjoy learning about different ways to learn languages.  I’ll keep learning how to help you, but I’ll be careful to double-check everything I say to make sure I don’t get confused.  I really want to do a good job helping you learn to speak."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Yeah. You have to learn the alphabet in the beginning and sometimes you can't even use the audio with the words. You have to read the text."}]
