DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How can I get better at painting?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’d recommend following tutorials online and in books and practicing by trying different techniques in different media.  It’s useful to talk with other people in person about your own paintings too, to see how your work compares to theirs.  I suggest painting portraits and animals, as these are both relatively simple and require painting things that other people understand.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I will try to paint different subjects and try different techniques to get better.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'What are some subjects you’d like to paint?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Maybe different landscapes. I could try to watch some old Bob Ross videos and try to paint along with him.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Good plan!  I’ll ask you a few times more about which paintings you want to do in the next week or so.  Will that be okay?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Sure, I'll let you know if I make any progress."}]
