DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I'm trying to have better dental hygiene. Can you tell me what are the benefits of flossing?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Sure!  Dental floss is a form of plastic rope that is woven together with string, like a piece of fabric, so it's safe to use for cleaning your teeth."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Right. Go on!'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Flossing with dental floss is a really effective way to clean between the teeth and the gum line.  If you are not using floss then you are likely to find that you are able to get food debris between the teeth and gums that would otherwise be cleaned by flossing, which can increase the chances of developing an oral cavity infection, commonly called gum disease or periodontal disease.  The infection caused by bacteria in the gums can spread to other parts of the body, such as the heart.  It can cause high blood pressure, increased heart rates, and other heart related diseases.  So it is a good idea to do some flossing at least once a day to keep these problems under control.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Wow, some of those things sound really dangerous'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "There’s a chance you could develop some gum disease if you don't floss your teeth, so yes, you really need to do it."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'So it helps with gum disease, avoiding cavities, helping the heart. What about bad breath?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'What kind of bad breath are you talking about?  Maybe a tooth brushing will solve that.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Typical bad breath? What other kind of bad breath exists?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do you know if your dog has been bit by a tick?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Let’s assume that you know you have a dog and you haven’t seen one on her.  Then, the usual thing to do would be to search for ticks.  Can you describe what this might look like?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'The dog has a red bump. How would I know if it is a tick bite?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, that would be a good clue.  If you find a tick, then you would need to try to remove it from your dog with tweezers or your fingers, by grabbing it close to the skin.  If you do that, it might appear white, a dead tick.  Or it might still be alive, with its head attached.  The head of a tick is larger than the part that latches onto a dog.  It’s very important to remove the entire body, or the tick will start to feed again.  If you can see the head attached, then you should try to remove it.  If the head is hidden, then it might be dangerous to try to remove it, because it might accidentally pinch the dog’s skin, leaving open wounds.  In these cases you can call your veterinarian for help.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Thank you for the tips. What if you can't see the tick though? I only see a bump."}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What should I consider when making a loan to a relative?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You have to consider whether you want to help your relative succeed. If you lend them money, and they lose it, they won’t be as able to afford rent, food, and all the things they need to live. So if you loan them money, and they fail to repay you, you won’t get your money back.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, and that could hurt our relationship, right?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Maybe, yes.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'All right, anything else I should consider?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You should also consider whether you think it’s safe to loan your relative money.  For example, maybe you have reason to think they may lie to you about repaying the loan. Or maybe they have a history of poor financial decision-making.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I guess I do have to think about that.'}]
