DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'I want to start playing some JRPGs. What are the most popular ones?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I could name some games I think you’d enjoy. There are three different styles of gameplay that you might find useful to distinguish: main series (most popular), spin-offs, and second-generation sequels. The main series games are the most prolific and well-known. There are, however, also spin-offs that are just as enjoyable and have had varying levels of popularity. The second-generation games are part of a major storyline that is so convoluted that its only coherent for the original creators. These games have been adapted into main series titles, and some spin-offs have also been remade as main series titles.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I know that Final Fantasy is a well-known JRPG. Do you think that's a good title to start with?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The original Final Fantasy on the NES is a well-known JRPG. The main series games usually have a larger storyline and world and more polish than the spin-off games. There is also a prequel to the original Final Fantasy, Final Fantasy IV, and Final Fantasy VII is considered to be the first real entry into the “second generation”. Final Fantasy VII is very difficult and complex, so I’d recommend starting with the original game to see if you like it.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Do you know if the original NES game got a remake for one of the newer consoles?'}]
