DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Why is French spoken in Quebec?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It’s also commonly referred to as “Quebecois French”. It’s one of many varieties of French. French is a Romance language and it has always been spoken in what is now Canada, but in most of Canada, this was never a dominant language. Instead, it was originally second language, but then became the dominant language in Quebec, where there were also laws in favor of French. It’s hard to say if there would be a similar “surge” in French elsewhere, but some scholars do think that French will become more widespread in North America in the future.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, can you tell me anything else?'}]
