DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How does ruby on rails work?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Ruby on Rails (RoR) is a web application framework, often referred to as a “web framework”.  It provides various tools for web developers, such as automatic database structure creation, and helpers to allow for easy rendering of HTML and other web content.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How long does it take to learn?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'There are many guides to learning RoR online.  It’s possible to learn in a week or two, though it can be difficult to get the hang of without a mentor or teacher.  It’s also possible to learn as much as you want on your own, though there will be additional resources you could benefit from.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Would you need to have experience with any other frameworks or coding experience to learn the basic concepts of RoR?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'RoR is a very high-level web framework, which means it will be easier to learn and will require less experience with other frameworks or coding languages.  I think it would be good for you to at least know some HTML and CSS, but if you don’t you’ll be able to pick it up just fine.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Are HTML and CSS basic development skills?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do corals get food?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Most corals are photosynthetic, which means that they convert sunlight into sugars that they then use for food.  Many corals also have tentacles, so they’ll sometimes go out to hunt for plankton.  But most of the time, the coral can get all the food it needs by photosynthesizing, or by eating what’s already attached to its body.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is their relationship to zooxanthellae'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The zooxanthellae live inside the coral, and help it by providing sugars that are derived from the food the coral eats.  The zooxanthellae themselves get everything they need from the coral, including sunlight and sugar, and also help the coral stay healthy by removing harmful waste products.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Do they need to photosynthesize food?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, every coral species that lives on land needs to photosynthesize.  Some also hunt for prey, like zooxanthellae or plankton.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Does this mean that corals are plants?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I make a cobb salad?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You could start by making a brown or white toast, in which you cook it in a pan on the stove. Then you would add some sundried tomatoes and capers and olive oil, and mix the ingredients.  You would then top the toast with basil and sea salt.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "White toast doesn't go in a cobb salad"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Then what goes into the cobb salad?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'That is what I am trying to figure out, I want to make a cobb salad and need help on what would go in it.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sorry about that!  Are you trying to make a “celery cobb salad?”'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Yes'}]
