DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How can I deal with erectile dysfunction without pills'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You don’t need to buy drugs from illegal pharmacies, or be ashamed of using them.  You can take an online survey to ask a doctor about your symptoms.  I think he’d help you figure out the best ways to cope with ED, and recommend medication or other strategies.  He can also check for health conditions that may be contributing to your ED.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Any natural things that could help with it?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'There are many natural methods, as well as many things that work for some people, but don’t work for others.   I think the best way is to meet with a doctor who can provide individual attention and help you figure out what will work for you.  Medications or procedures can be effective if you have a good doctor, but you may also be interested in making lifestyle changes, or learning about therapy and behavioral treatments.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay Thanks'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How can I find an electrician to let me be his or her apprentice?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'If you’re in an urban environment, chances are you’ll be able to find the electrician in your area on the DoItYourself or Apple App Stores. And if you’re in a more rural area, then you can look for a trade school near you, or any nearby city where they offer trade school programs, and check if one of them has a course in electrician skills.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I want to work right away as an apprentice. I can work for free to start. An Apple App store? That has nothing to do with electricians.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It sounds like you need to learn more about the nature of apprenticeships.  Here’s what I could tell you: In the past, most apprenticeships were for “learn-by-doing”—rather than just asking an apprentice what skills they were good at, the apprentice got to try them out themselves, and learned skills by having to work with real-life materials.  Nowadays, though, there are apprenticeships with classroom and theory-learning requirements.  In fact, a lot of people are unhappy with apprenticeships today because they’re not being allowed to try out their work skills.  You might want to speak to someone at a trade school in your area about apprenticeships, and see if they can give you a good explanation of the current situation.  I could also explain more about apprenticeships, and offer any resources I know about, if you wanted to go into more depth.  Do you want me to go into more detail about apprenticeships?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'yes'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'In ancient times, apprentices were expected to work as a laborer and learn to do the work as they went along, with the master teaching them as they needed it.  Later, an apprentice was hired, put through a fixed course of instruction, and then certified to work for the master.  However, it turned out that this often lead to the apprentices having “the knowledge but not the skill”, that is, not really knowing how to do the job well, or really knowing how to do the job quickly and efficiently.  So then, apprentices began to be encouraged to do the job during the course of instruction, so that they could gain “the skill and the knowledge” of the trade.  The most recent innovation is for there to be a defined theoretical knowledge component to an apprenticeship, as well.  So, I think that the apprenticeship you’re interested in sounds like an apprenticeship that is traditional in most ways.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'yes'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "What's the best place to visit along the U.S coastline in the winter? I'd like to experience lots of snow, if possible."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The best place to see lots of snow would be along the border of Washington and Oregon. The mountains here are often snow-capped and the temperatures in winter are generally mild, especially if you go to the southern end of this region.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Sounds great! Is that kind of like Portland and Vancouver area?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Portland and Vancouver would both be great to visit!'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Okay. That sounds like a plan. What's the climate like there in winter?"}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What are ways to help someone sober up fast? Say they drank too much alcohol'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I don’t know much about alcohol, so I’m not sure what to tell you here, but I can say that for some people, a little coffee and some food might help.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay. Any kind of coffee or something really strong?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I know that a lot of people like espresso, and I’ve also heard of people doing “coffee enemas” to clean their stomachs. I don’t know if either of these might help or if it’s something you should do.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Not really sure how that applies to sobering up fast'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What kinds of milk options are dairy free?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Well there is nut milks, such as almond, coconut, or soy, which are great options. Or perhaps you can make rice milk, although it may be more expensive.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Lactose intolerant people can drink nut milks?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, that’s right. Nut milks are lactose free, as are some almond milk and some rice milk. There are also some other options, like soy milk and coconut milk, which are also lactose free.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Are nut milks as nutritious as regular milk?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Nut milks are less nutritious, as they are typically made from whole nuts.  They are fortified with vitamins, which is something that is important to people with allergies to dairy.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Which nut milk is the most popular?'}]
