DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What type of plywood is best for outdoor use?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'For exterior projects, it’s best to avoid wet or otherwise environmentally challenging locations.  We can recommend either exterior grade or weathered cedar plywood, with exterior grade being the lower cost choice.  For the inside of your house, cedar plywood is fine, but many interior projects use engineered wood instead of plywood.  The latter doesn’t require the periodic maintenance required for the exterior grade, and is better suited for environments where termites could be a problem.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'So is cedar plywood best for exterior use?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I gain confidence when asking someone out?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Well, I don’t think there’s a single “right way” to do that. But, my main recommendation would be to be honest about the situation you’re in, to explain why you want to ask someone out, and why that person is a good fit for you. Maybe even ask a friend to go with you.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Any other ideas?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sure, there’s a few. I think it’s important to pick the right situation, which means a private setting with no people around that you know to the extent that they would gossip about you.  And in many cases, it’s nice to go out for dinner or coffee first, if that person is not available for a long-term date in the short term.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'All right. What else can you tell me?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How can one deal with passive aggressive people?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Awareness of passive-aggressive people and their dynamics can be helpful in dealing with them. I think it would be helpful to first start with the notion of what a passive-aggressive person is, and what they’re like.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Well I know what it is and what they're like"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'OK, well let’s think about what it is that they’re doing, if you want to start there. I could describe it to you, if that would be helpful?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I'd rather just hear general tips on how to deal with a passive aggressive person"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The term “passive aggressive” is often used to refer to people who act in passive ways to avoid directly confronting conflict or issues, and who do not otherwise behave aggressively. The stereotypical example of passive-aggression is someone who wants to show their anger, but doesn’t want to own it and risk losing control. They have a choice about the passive way they take action, and it’s motivated by fear of conflict and anger. There is a debate around whether or not such behavior actually is aggressive or just defensive.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Ohhhh, wow, how did I not think about that before? So they are passive aggressive because they fear actually confronting, so they do it passively?'}]
