DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Hey! I have some friends who only wash their hair once or twice a week. I hear that this is better for my overall hair health but my hair only stays looking good for 1-2 days and then it looks greasy and dried out. Is there any strategies you have for me to keep my hair healthier between washes?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I am glad to hear that your friends are keeping their hair so healthy! But I do think that you should go for a wash once a week. This is when the dirt from the hair follicles is scraped off, which is where dirt and oil is stored. I think the greasy look you describe is probably from the natural oils in your scalp leaking out, which are produced in a healthy scalp. But if you shampoo your hair every day, there isn’t enough time for these oils to build up and stick to the hair follicles, and also a lot of your natural oils will be washed off.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is there anything I can do besides dry shampoo between washes to help my natural oils do their thing?'}]
