g, you can usually just fold down the top of the mattress and place the mattress pad directly onto the mattress.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Any other advice?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You should also check for “stretch marks” or “contusions” on the mattress.  These are places where the mattress has pulled apart and looks deformed.  This is usually caused by the mattress sinking down the box spring over time, which can be a symptom of sagging.  If you see this, you should bring it to the attention of a mattress store salesperson, who should take care of the problem.  You should also change your bed linens and make sure they’re still crisp and clean.  This can also keep your mattress looking good.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Any other ideas?'}]
