roughout its history.\n\nIf you have any more questions, feel free to ask! 😊", "</think>\n\nYou're welcome! Have a wonderful Thanksgiving! 🐔✨", "</think>\n\nOkay, the user asked for some curly-haired dogs, but then changed their mind and said they don't need to be funny. So I need to adjust the response to focus on the curly-haired aspect without adding humor.\n\nFirst, I should list some common curly-haired dog breeds. The Curly-Coated Collie is a classic example, known for their thick, woolly coats. Then there's the Curly-Coated Retriever, which is also a good candidate. Maybe mention the Curly-Coated Poodle, though they're more associated with the Poodle breed. Also, the Curly-Coated German Shepherd could be another one, though they might not be as common.\n\nI should also consider other breeds. The Curly-Coated Chihuahua is a fun one, but maybe the user wants more of a standard breed. The Curly-Coated Boxer might be another option. Oh, and the Curly-Coated Doberman. But I need to", "</think>\n\nPreparing for a first child is a journey that starts long before you even bring the baby home. It's a mix of physical, emotional, and practical preparations. Here are some key steps to help you mentally prepare for a new baby:\n\n---\n\n### **1. Emotional Preparation**\n- **Accept the Change**: Your life is going to change in ways you may not yet fully understand. You may feel overwhelmed, excited, or even scared. Be kind to yourself.\n- **Embrace the New Life**: The arrival of a baby brings a new chapter of your life, full of love, joy, and connection.\n- **Allow Yourself to Feel**: It’s okay to have mixed feelings—sometimes you might feel overwhelmed, and at other times, you might feel elated. It’s a natural part of the journey.\n- **Find a Support System**: Talk to friends, family, or a trusted professional (like a pediatrician or counselor). You don’t have to do this alone.\n\n---\n\n"]
