DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you tell me the basics of travel insurance?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sure! Here’s a list of things I can tell you:  \n1.    You can purchase travel insurance to protect yourself against financial loss in case you’re a victim of a disaster (this is called a ‘disaster policy’), which can include situations like flight delays, cancellations, robbery, lost luggage, and theft of valuables or cash.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you expand more on your first point?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sure. I can tell you the importance of travel insurance, and how you might want to think about it. I can also explain how much insurance costs, and what plans you might be eligible for.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Well, I wanted to you tell me more about a disaster policy.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'A disaster policy usually pays for losses that you incur because of an unexpected disaster, like a hurricane, wildfire, or the 2008 earthquake in China. You may find that a travel insurance company offers coverage for several different kinds of disasters, like fire, flood, theft, hurricane, earthquake, terrorism, and accident.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is there any disaster you can think of that they would not cover? I mean, they pretty much cover all disasters, it seems'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I guess the only thing you really need to make sure of is that the travel insurance company will cover your destination.  So let’s say you’re going to visit Hong Kong, and there’s a typhoon at the same time you’re there, and you lose your luggage. Then you could find out that the travel insurance company is only licensed to provide coverage in Hong Kong, and you could make sure that if you wanted to buy insurance, you’d need to contact the insurance company to see if they would cover your trip.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Got it. So make sure they cover the specific area I'm traveling to."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yep. Also, make sure they’re licensed to insure you in your destination country, because it would be a problem if they weren’t.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Right.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Is there anything else you wanted to know about travel insurance?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'No'}]
