DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I make sourdough starter?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'To make sourdough starter, you need some wheat flour, water, and a container.  Flour alone is a great medium for growing bacteria, so you can just add some flour, water, and a lid to a container, and let it sit.  We can make sourdough starter together: we’ll prepare the flour and water and then put them in a covered container, in the back corner of your kitchen (you can also do this outside). We’ll check on it every few days to stir it, and once it has enough bubbles and smells yeasty, we’ll scoop some out and use it to make some bread.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Wow, I didn't know it was so easy."}]
