red list of duties, here's a concise and comprehensive overview:\n\n---\n\n### **Main Duties of a Handyman**\n\n1. **General Maintenance and Repairs**  \n   - Fix leaks, fix plumbing, fix electrical systems  \n   - Repair and replace broken or damaged items (doors, windows, faucets, etc.)  \n   - Fix and maintain HVAC systems and heating units  \n   - Repair and install plumbing fixtures and pipes  \n\n2. **Home Improvement and Renovation**  \n   - Install new flooring, walls, or countertops  \n   - Repair or build furniture (e.g., assembling or painting furniture)  \n   - Fix or replace windows, doors, and locks  \n   - Perform basic electrical and wiring work  \n\n3. **Interior and Exterior Work**  \n   - Clean and maintain floors, bathrooms, and kitchens  \n   - Paint walls", '</think>\n\nBeing more empathetic to your friends is a meaningful and valuable goal. Here are some practical steps and strategies that can help you become more empathetic and understanding:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **Practice Active Listening**\n- **Listen fully** without interruptions or distractions. Let your friend know you\'re focused and care about what they\'re saying.\n- **Reflect and acknowledge** their feelings and thoughts. For example, you can say, "That must be really tough right now."\n- **Ask open-ended questions** to encourage them to share more: "What did you feel when you said that?"\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Practice Self-Awareness**\n- **Reflect on your own emotions** and how they might affect your interactions with your friends.\n- **Ask yourself questions** like: Do I feel jealous or frustrated when they are happy? Am I being over-sensitive?\n- **Stay open-minded** and avoid judgment. Try to understand the perspective of your friends.\n\n---\n\n### 3.', "</think>\n\nThat's a great and thoughtful question! Learning about the **working of political systems** is a fantastic goal, and it's definitely a journey that takes time and curiosity. Here’s a structured way to explore the **branche