ce** and can **shape the direction of policies**, **economics**, and **international relations** in a given area or group.\n\n### 📌 Key Features:\n1. **Dominant Influence**: The hegemon has the **most power** in the region or system.\n2. **Policy Shaping**: The hegemon influences **international laws**, **governance**, and **global politics**.\n3. **Economic and Political Control**: They can dictate trade agreements, set policies, and often act as a **powerful leader**.\n4. **Ideological Influence**: Hegemonies can shape **global ideas** and values.\n\n###"]
