DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you help me prepare for an earthquake?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I would be happy to help.  What sort of help are you looking for?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What do I need to be prepared with in the event of an earthquake'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Do you have a kit with food, water, flashlights and batteries?  How long do you have food and water for?  How long do you have electricity for?  Will you have some battery-powered radios?  Are you confident that you know how to use them?  What sort of medical kit do you have?  Do you have a working fire extinguisher?  Is it possible to move people out of their homes, at least temporarily?  Do you have a shelter in a safe location?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, so those are some things I would need, food, water flashlights and batteries. What kind of food?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It depends on the length of the outage.  For a short outage (a couple of days), maybe one bag of each: fruit, veggies, cereal, a jar of peanut butter and crackers, and a few cans of soup.  For a long outage (more than a week), you would want at least two weeks’ worth of food.  Do you have that much?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What kind of food would I need with me for a long outage?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The more varied the better.  You’ll be able to eat a much wider variety of foods that way.  So the more variety, the better.  Ideally you’d want a variety of proteins, starchy vegetables and fruit, and sweets.  And dried food, since things like milk, butter, and eggs would be spoiled after a while.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Well, vegetables and fruits go bad after like a week without refrigeration'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Fresh veggies and fruits would be a very short term emergency food.  Can you keep them in the fridge for a couple of days at most, with no power?  What about frozen veggies?  Do you have a way to store them?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I'm not sure sure. A long outage means no refrigeration. The only thing that works is canned stuff"}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "Hi, it's my dream to direct a film. How can I make that dream a reality?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "This is a pretty cool question. If you want to make films, you should watch other films and read books about filmmaking and watch other filmmakers' movies. You can go to film school for classes and workshops, which would help you build your knowledge and prepare you for a career in filmmaking. You should also talk with your friends and family members who might know people who are in the film industry, to see if you could get advice or a job as an intern or apprentice.  My guess is you'll want to read about how filmmaking works and get familiar with the different tools that are used, like cameras, lighting and editing software.  You should also find out about how people get paid to make films and how you can fund your projects, since the cost of making films can be very high.  You might try joining a filmmaking club to meet people who know about filmmaking, and you can see if you can get support to make your own films.  I hope this advice helps you!"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, those all seem like sound suggestions. How about some nuts and bolts stuff - how do I get financing for a film?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'My mom has been suffering from sciatica for a long time and its not getting better. Is there anything she can do?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’m sorry to hear that, I really hope you can figure out a good solution.  Sciatica is an inflammation of the sciatic nerve, which is a nerve that runs from the lower back, down to the legs.  When there’s an injury or degenerative disorder in the lower back or leg joints, there can be pressure on the sciatic nerve which causes sciatica.  Since you’ve already been looking for a solution and she hasn’t gotten better, maybe you could consider getting some surgery done?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "She has thought about that, but she read that surgery often doesn't work. Is this true?"}]
