DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Could you help me learn about the Intervention of Haiti in 1994?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sure, I’ll take a look!'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I would like some general information on the event.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sure! There were military and paramilitary forces involved in the invasion, which resulted in a peace treaty that led to the restoration of Haiti’s sovereignty.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Who was the United States President during this Intervention?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It was Bill Clinton. He led the Operation Uphold Democracy and Operation Support Democracy, that included troops from the US, Canada, France and the Dominican Republic.  President Clinton led this operation after 12 years of coups in Haiti, this invasion was officially described as “Operation Uphold Democracy.”  While the military didn’t disband the Haitian military, they did “decommission” the Presidential Guard, the Haitian Army, and Navy, the only armed bodies that Haitian military had.  The operation was known for the thousands of civilians killed in military strikes and the large-scale massacres by paramilitary forces.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How many years long did this intervention last?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is a late fee on a credit card and how do you avoid them?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Late fees are charged by the bank on which you have the credit card, and generally are a percentage of the amount you owe.  The bank doesn’t want to lose money, so they want to ensure that they get paid for the money you owe.  A common practice is to add on a monthly “interest” fee which continues to accrue until you pay the debt off.  As a general rule, it’s better to avoid late fees, since they can quickly eat into your credit score.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "So if you don't pay on time then they charge the late fee?"}]
