DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How did they decide on the height of the basket for basketball.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Basketball began as a game called YMCA International Training School, in Springfield, Massachusetts in 1892, which was played on an indoor wooden floor. In 1896, Dr. James Naismith, the instructor at the school, began to experiment with a game which he called “Duck on a Rock”. He would throw a basketball through a hoop, attempting to land it in a peach basket. The team that scored the most points, after playing for 15 minutes, would be the winner. His goal was to find a way to get more people to play. When he decided to change the name of the game to “Basket Ball”, he asked his friend, Sumner Archibald to come up with a set of rules. Sumner Archibald was an avid bicyclist, and had an interest in mathematics.  He put together a set of rules for the game, which included the following:'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Wow! That is a lot of information. Do you know how high they make the basket off the ground?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, the NBA has not specified how high they want the basketball hoop to be, but most of them are about 10 ft.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'No real regulation, eh?'}]
