 fun, creative way to describe a low-carb, healthy dessert that you can make with ingredients like:\n\n- Low-carb or non-dairy milk (like almond or oat milk)\n- Low-carb or keto-friendly sweeteners (like erythritol, monk fruit, or stevia)\n- Low-carb flour (like almond flour or coconut flour)\n- Low-carb or no-sugar-added-ingredients (if you\'re going for the "fluff" part)\n- Maybe some cocoa powder for a decadent touch (if you\'re going for the "fluff" part)\n\nAnd yes, you can', "</think>\n\nThat's a lot! Watching four hours of TV a day is significantly more than the average. Most people watch around 2 to 3 hours of TV each day, so four hours is on the higher side. \n\nHere are a few things to consider:\n\n1. **Screen Time and Health**: Prolonged screen time can affect your sleep, focus, and mental health. It's important to balance screen time with physical activity, face-to-face interaction, and hobbies.\n\n2. **Addiction and Mental Health**: Excessive TV watching can lead to addiction, anxiety, and a lack of motivation. It can also affect your social skills and communication.\n\n3. **Physical Health**: Watching TV can reduce physical activity, which can lead to issues like lack of exercise, poor posture, and even obesity.\n\n4. **Quality of Content**: Not all TV content is the same. If you're watching shows that are not educational or interesting, it could be contributing to a lack of motivation"]
