DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do you help a dog that has anxiety?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'If you look in the Q&A section of this help page, you can find an entry that describes an evidence-based therapy for helping anxious dogs.  The therapy involves teaching your dog to relax by means of repetition, mental imagery, and distraction, and they can all be learned in the training videos on this site.  If you’re interested in learning more about your dog’s behavior, the videos also give you a chance to investigate that further.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I would really like that but I can't see the videos."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'If you don’t see the videos, there could be a few reasons for that. First, it could be that your screen resolution is too low. Second, you might be on a mobile phone which has very limited web capabilities. Lastly, it might be because your browser has an issue. In these cases, if you’d like to, you can adjust the settings in your browser to allow you to see the video.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I still can't see it though."}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I check for lice?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The usual methods are combing the hair with a special, fine comb, or using a special flashlight and magnifying glass or a microscope.  This should also be used to check for other parasites like mites and ticks.  Sometimes checking hair just for lice, even without other parasites, is enough to control the infestation.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What should I do if I find lice?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It’s very important to eliminate the lice as soon as possible!   It is also helpful to do a treatment once every 2 weeks or once a month to keep the number of lice low, so that the treatment doesn’t hurt the head.   The best treatment for lice is to wash the head with a special shampoo, or apply it directly from a bottle.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Should I keep my child out of school if he has lice?'}]
