DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I make my own hot sauce?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'What sort of hot sauce do you want?  There are several types of peppers that can be used, and various recipes for making them.  Which are you interested in making?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I'm not sure. For now I would like something that is tasty and easy to make."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'As a recommendation, I would recommend cayenne, which is one of the most common hot sauces, made by crushing dried cayenne peppers.  If you don’t mind its very spicy flavor, it’s very easy to make.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay what do I need to make cayenne pepper hot sauce?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You could purchase the dried peppers from a grocery store and crush them yourself, or try one of the recipes found online, or for a quick way to start, I suggest the Food.com recipe that uses a blender.  I can also tell you about the different ways that you could turn cayenne peppers into a sauce, and what each one is good for.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I want to turn it into some kind of sauce. How do I do that?'}]
