DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What are some good artists from the 1920s?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Alright, I can give you some suggested names and a description of their artwork.  The painter Vincent Van Gogh was an important artist in the late 1800s, who focused on what we call “Expressionist” art.  He believed that the artist should reflect their feelings in their art, rather than trying to describe them.  That means that there will often be very high emotion or intensity in his paintings.  And an interesting result of this is that some people don’t really like Van Gogh’s paintings.  For instance, when you Google his painting The Starry Night, you’ll see lots of people sharing photos of it on social media saying things like “I hate this painting” and “It’s gross.”  Other people find the high emotion of the painting intriguing or refreshing, and enjoy it.  So when thinking about a Van Gogh painting, keep in mind that he might have painted something you find exciting, but other people might find it upsetting.  For instance, let’s say you found the painting Starry Night exciting.  Some of the other paintings I’ll mention could be similar to Starry Night, so be prepared to see some pretty intense artworks.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, I meant musical artists.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Musical artists who were active in the 1920s?  They tend to get remembered as the musicians of the 20s because music was just beginning to be recorded.  Not all the musicians were famous then, but most of them became popular later.  I’ll tell you a little bit about each, and you can look at the rest on your own time.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I know there were some.'}]
