DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I'm trying to find out more information on President Andrew Johnson, can you help?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'President Johnson was the President of the United States between 1865 and 1869.  He came into office during a time of intense controversy in the United States over the meaning of the war, the future of the Union, and the new president.  President Johnson was a southerner and a former slave owner and many saw him as an example of a person who would represent their interests.  Many of the Republicans who had been the party of Lincoln found this very offensive, and a divide in the country began.  The U.S. Supreme Court had several decisions on the constitutionality of the amendments passed during the war, and the decisions were read before congress in December 1865.  President Johnson reacted very negatively to this, and the congressional session was marked by harsh speech and even physical violence.  This only worsened the divisions between Republicans and Democrats, who were split over whether or not the amendments should be approved.  The debates in congress were particularly well-known because of the reporters who published them in the New York Times.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "What was one of President Johnson's major accomplishments as president?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "He served on the civil rights commission, and there he used his power to put an end to slavery in the south.  He also worked to get the Freedmen’s Bureau to distribute food and aid to freed slaves.  He also helped to create a judicial system that treated the freed slaves fairly.  In 1870, he promoted the Amnesty Act, which restored the voting rights to most Southerners who had fought on the Confederacy's side.  Some of these leaders re-joined their states' political lives, though they could not resume their old political roles.  President Johnson supported a program of reconstruction for the Southern states, which was meant to address many of the problems that the country faced after the war."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What political party was he apart of when he was President?'}]
