DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'My friend wants to join the USA military. Is there an age limit? Can you get too old?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'That depends on which branch of the military, and on the circumstances. Generally, yes, a person can get too old. In general, age 18 is the minimum age for enlistment.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How about being 40? is that too old?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It’s possible, though unlikely. If you’re talking about a person with a good health, strength, and training they should be able to serve.  Again, it’s hard to make any hard and fast rules, but the Pentagon tends to be reluctant to accept someone who’s nearing age 40.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I guess I can understand why. Us old people are slow to learn.'}]
