DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What are some things I should know about fostering a pet?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I see that you’re asking about fostering a pet!  That is a great idea, and it’s not that difficult to do.\nFostering a pet is a way of looking after a pet for someone else, and so a lot of pets that would otherwise have no good place to live find homes when people foster them.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Where can I go to get a pet to foster?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Well there are a variety of places that will help you get a pet. For example, some of the shelters or rescue centers have pets available for fostering.  There are also organizations that will match you with an animal that needs fostering.  There are also a variety of online sources that will help you to find a pet for fostering.  Does any of this sound helpful to you?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is there a way to be less attached to the pet I am fostering?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What does the Department of Agriculture do?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The USDA is responsible for a number of things.  They’re a big part of developing the US agricultural and rural economy, including managing foreign trade. They also support food and nutrition research and environmental protection.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do they support food?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'They offer programs to help farmers grow and produce food. They offer crop insurance for farmers who take on extra risk, and disaster assistance for farmers in disaster areas. They run food assistance programs, like food stamps and school lunches. They also operate the food safety and inspection system to make sure we have good food.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Well we all need good food.'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Why do I cramp and feel tired during my period'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'If you mean you feel exhausted during the menstrual period, you may have an iron deficiency, which is an imbalance of your levels of iron in your blood.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I got tested and iron is normal level. I do have a few small cysts and might have endometriosis'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You might have a small endometriosis problem. But for most women, bleeding during your period usually isn’t related to medical issues.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Very true. Ty for your insight! Nity nite'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I started working night shift so I have to sleep during the day. But it's noisy and bright out. What can I use to get better sleep?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "I was wondering if you’ve thought about getting some darker curtains or drapes, or a sleep mask?  I find that it's much easier to sleep if it's darker and quieter."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Those are a good start, thanks!'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'how do i stop my kids from saying bad words?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How can I get a better nights rest'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'In my experience, a glass of water around an hour before bed time can help with sleep.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'anything else that could help?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The human sleep cycle follows a certain pattern.  After waking up, your body enters a phase of deep sleep, which happens more frequently during the early morning hours and lasts approximately 15-20 minutes.  It has a very slow heart rate and the eyes are closed.  That’s the ideal time to relax, and some people may consider it to be the most restful phase.  Next is the REM phase, which starts around an hour after deep sleep and lasts for about an hour.  During this phase, your eyes move quickly, and your breathing becomes erratic.  This is the ideal time to let the mind and body unwind from the daily stresses of the day, so many people feel rested after it.  Once that phase is over, the last stage of sleep, or slow wave sleep, begins.  Here, the heart rate and breathing become slow and steady again, and you may even fall asleep for a few minutes.  After a couple of hours of this phase, your body will likely wake you up, and that’s when you’ll be ready for the day.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'okay thanks'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What are some snacks 8 month olds can enjoy?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Salty foods are a good choice as it can help build your baby’s immune system.  Why not try pickles, olives, peas, sunflower seeds, edamame beans, and sweet potato fries?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, cool. Any other advice?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Well, if you want to encourage your child to try new foods and experiences, it helps to involve other people. For example, if you invite your child’s favorite caregiver to a party, you can get them to enjoy trying new foods.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "It's about the every day, not just a party."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, I realize that. In fact, just like any child would, 8 month olds are pretty distracted and forgetful. To help keep your child motivated to try new foods, have as much fun as possible at mealtimes. Keep your child company and make the experience an enjoyable one. If your child has a favorite toy, include it at the table so they are interested in eating what you are serving them.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, that makes sense'}]
