DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What does wage garnishment mean?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '“Garnishment” is a legal procedure where the government can force a person to give money to another person, usually by court order, when that person is involved in some legal dispute.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'So they take their money before they even get it?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What are the pros and cons of the native reservation system in the United States?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'That is an excellent question, and one I don’t know all that much about.  I’m going to do my best to pull up some information on that topic, but there are a couple of different ways I could get this information, and they can both be useful.  I can look up some credible sources and collect facts in a summary form, and summarize them for you.  This could be called a “database” and could be in any form, though typically it’s written down in a text file or online document.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I\'ll get you started. On one hand, the reservation system allocates native americans land where they can continue their culture. On the negative side, natives don\'t actually "own" their reservation land, and as a result of being on reservations and not paying taxes, they often times don\'t have many resources on their reservations.'}]
