DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "What does escrow mean when you're buying a house?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Escrow means that the seller agrees to hold money that will be used to pay off the mortgage at a certain point.  In return, the buyer agrees to pay a certain percentage of the cost of the house upfront, and the buyer can’t take possession of the house until the seller agrees that the home has been paid for.  If there are any problems with the deal, the buyer can go back to escrow and get their money back.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Do you have escrow until your loan is paid off?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'If my bank loan was a mortgage, I would, since that’s a common example of escrow.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'When was escrow invented?'}]
