\n\n---\n\n### **1. Rule of Thumb: Screen Size (inches)**\nA common rule of thumb is to use **1.5 times the width of the room** for the TV size. For example:\n\n- **Small living room (20–30 sq ft)**:  \n  - **Best size**: 50–65 inches.  \n  - *Reason*: 50–65 inches fits most small rooms (average TV sizes for 30–40 sq ft are 55–65 inches).  \n  - For a 20–30 sq ft room, a **55-inch** TV is often ideal.\n\n- **Medium living room", '</think>\n\nThe longest-serving monarch in the world is **King Charles III** of the United Kingdom. He has been the King of England, Scotland, Wales, and Northern Ireland since **2022**, when he ascended the throne following the death of his father, King Charles II, who died in 2022.\n\n### Key Points:\n- **King Charles III** has been the **King of the United Kingdom** since **2022**.\n- He was previously the **King of the United Kingdom** from **1649 to 1650** (during the English Civil War), and he was the **King of England and Wales** from **1649 to 1650**.\n- His reign began in **2022**, making him the **longest-serving monarch** in the world as of now.\n\n### Duration of Reign:\n- **From 1649 to 1650**:', '</think>\n\nSunflowers are a large and diverse group of flowering plants in the genus *Helianthus*, commonly known as sunflowers. They are part of the family Asteraceae (the daisy family) and are widely cultivated for their seeds, which are used in edible oil, margarine, and other products.\n\n### Types of Sunflowers:\n\n1. **Common Sunflower (*Helianthus annuus*)**:\n   - The most widely cultivated species.\n   - Native to the Americas.\n   - Includes varieties like *H. annuus* var. *annuus* (common sunflower) and *H. annuus* var. *glabrum* (smooth seed sunflower).\n   - Produces large, bright yellow flowers and edible seeds.\n\n2. **Smooth Seed Sunflower (*Helianthus annuus* var. *glabrum*)**:\n   - Also known as the "smooth seed" or "smooth" sunflower.\n']
