DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How does adding the federal oil reserve to the oil market help to lower the price of gas?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’m glad you asked! Adding more oil to the oil market increases supply. This reduces the price of oil.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'So the more oil for sale the less they can sell it for?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'That’s right. The price of gas decreases when there’s more supply, as more drivers can drive and so they need less gas to fill their tanks.  We might say that the more oil for sale, the “cheaper” gas becomes.  But there are many factors affecting the price of gas, so some prices are lower even without adding oil, and other prices are higher.  But overall prices have decreased over time.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Alright. So it makes gas worth less if everyone has it?'}]
