DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is it safe to vacation to Thailand?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Thailand is generally considered to be quite safe, although some natural disasters may occur.  There are also frequent outbreaks of dengue and malaria in southern Thailand.  It is advisable to wear insect repellent and to wear light-colored clothing, especially in the afternoon.  Also, be careful in the rainy season when mosquitos are more active, especially if you stay in the provinces of Chachoengsao or Phetchaburi.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you get vaccinated for dengue and malaria?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, but the vaccine is not always recommended.  The CDC recommends the vaccine for people over 1 year of age and the CDC advises against the vaccine for travelers to Cambodia.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'But I am not going to Cambodia.'}]
