DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is the USPS actually mentioned in the Constitution?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, it is.  Article 1, Section 8 of the Constitution defines the postal system of the United States.  The Postal Service was not established as an independent agency until 1792.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is it supposed to turn a profit?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The Postal Service is mandated to provide universal service to every address in the US, a few select international addresses, and is allowed to operate at a deficit.  Currently it is about 30 billion dollars in debt, but it is expected to make a profit in the near future.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "What would we do if there wasn't a USPS any longer?"}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I'd like to soothe a friend of mine, who skinned their knee. Do you have any helpful suggestions?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sounds painful!  How about some ice?  Would that help?  I think ice is the first thing people usually reach for.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Might be. They got the wound covered up and the bandaged. I wonder what some supportive actions might be for my friend?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I see.  Supportive actions like... hugs and kisses and other social rituals to show your friend that you care.  Is that what you had in mind?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "You're getting closer. I was wondering if I should bring them food, or run errands for them maybe?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Ah, you could run errands for them or cook for them. Or if you don’t feel comfortable with any of those things, you could ask them if there’s anything you could do to make them feel better, and they can tell you specifically what they want from you.  If they don’t know yet, I’d suggest you ask them that way.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'That could be helpful. I appreciate the suggestions.'}]
