DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'I like to host guests at my home from time to time, and I am gathering  recipes of different dishes and drinks to keep things interesting. I am interested in trying some Ghanaian dishes. Can you give me a recipe for Waakye?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sure! Waakye is a staple dish in Ghanaian culture, and comes in a number of varieties. If you’re interested in something relatively traditional, it would be a stew of ground beef, tomatoes, onion, and coriander leaves, served with a side of jollof rice.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you provide a vegan friendly recipe?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sure. So it’s made with garlic, ginger, onions, red bell peppers, tomatoes, and spices like cinnamon, cumin, coriander, and allspice, and served over rice. It doesn’t have to be vegan-friendly, but I could make sure that it’s possible to make it vegan.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I thought Waakye traditionally has beans and rices. Is there any reason why you have excluded the beans from the recipe you provided?'}]
