DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I make popcorn without a microwave?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '“Most popcorn that you buy in stores is cooked at high temperatures for about 20 seconds in a small metal pan.  This browns the outside and cooks the inside.  Sometimes microwave ovens cook popcorn using the same method of cooking, with an 8-cup microwave.”'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'It will only take 20 seconds to pop on the stovetop?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes. Just find a medium-sized pot (the size of your microwave) and place it on the stove.  You can use some corn kernels to test how hot it is, by touching them to the bottom of the pot.  For normal popcorn, the point is to get the popcorn popping (or crackling).  When the pot is hot enough to pop the corn, put in the popcorn and cover the pot.  Wait for 10-20 seconds, then take the lid off.  You’ll know it’s done if the popping has stopped.  Then take the pot off the heat.  The popcorn will taste better if you put a small amount of oil in the pot first, to prevent the popcorn from sticking.  And you can season it with salt, butter, or margarine.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Okay hopefully I won't burn the popcorn."}]
