DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is the New York Stock Exchange?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The New York Stock Exchange is an American exchange and the largest in the world.  It is an open-outcry market, so shares are traded in a public meeting in which prices are quoted in a designated market segment.  Shares are traded by dealers on the exchange floor, using a system of a virtual auction, while most of the trading is done by phone, on the trading floor and in the dealers’ offices.  The NYSE has more than 8,000 companies listed on it and over 200 listed with the symbols.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is the exchange floor still active?  Most people trade using the internet nowadays.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'That’s right.  The floor is still active.  But the trading floor is much smaller than it was back in the 1970s, and most transactions are done over the phone.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can the public visit the floor of the stock exchange?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Oh, yes!  You can go to the exchange floor and watch the floor traders in action.  You will find it very interesting.  It’s a place where history is being made.  The open-outcry of the floor gives an extra level of excitement to the experience.  People can learn a lot by watching the traders, and you can take selfies with them too!'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'According to the information I got online, the exchange is no longer accessible to the public.  So, your information was not up to date.'}]
