DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'I plan to make meatballs to eat with spaghetti.  Do you have a good recipe?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Great!  It sounds like you want to make something savory, which will be covered by the food category.  The recipe search engine we have here can help find meats that go well together, and also have some additional guidance about using various spices and herbs in sauces.  Did you know that the English word “meatball” comes from the Italian word “mussolina,” which literally translates to “moss balls”?  Moss was a common ingredient in breads and sauces in the ancient world.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'No, I did not know the Italian word.  Now I know.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I see, and I hope that helps!  So you want to know about making meatballs that go well with spaghetti, and perhaps also about cooking meatballs.  Here is a recipe for meatballs covered with a simple sauce, and I’ll do my best to give you a high-quality result.  The “tri-tip steak” should be mixed with beef, pork, garlic and other things before being shaped into meatballs.  The sauce for the meatballs can be made with tomatoes, butter and bread crumbs, and then some herbs to go with the spaghetti you plan to eat.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'This time I will make the meatballs.  Tomorrow I will make the spaghetti sauce.  Please give me a list of ingredients I need to make meatballs.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It sounds like you want to make something savory, which will be covered by the food category.  The recipe search engine we have here can help find meats that go well together, and also have some additional guidance about using various spices and herbs in sauces.  Did you know that the English word “meatball” comes from the Italian word “mussolina,” which literally translates to “moss balls”?  Moss was a common ingredient in breads and sauces in the ancient world.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'You have not given me the list of ingredients yet.'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I'm new to wearing makeup, but really want to make my eyes standout."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "I'm excited to hear that!  Let me give you some advice!"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Ok, how do I make my eyes standout?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'That depends on how you want to do it.  If you want them to stand out to others, you can try using a darker-colored shadow to set off the eyes.  If you want your eyes to stand out to yourself, the best approach is to draw the lines that you think are most important to accentuate your features.  If you do it this way, your eyes will look better to others and also to yourself.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What other makeup products should I use besides shadow?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "In general, you'll probably want to stick to basic shades that work with most skin tones.  You can use darker or lighter shades, but for the most part you want to start with something simple and easy to manage.  If you're going for a bold look, choose darker colors.  If you want to bring out the shape of your face, it's okay to choose brighter colors."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Any other products specifically for eyes'}]
