ay! 😊", "</think>\n\nThe Eiffel Tower was constructed from **1887 to 1889**, during the **Exposition Universelle** (World's Fair) in **1889**, which was held in **Paris** to honor the **100th anniversary of the French Revolution**. It was designed by **Hippolyte François Eiffel** and constructed by **a team of engineers and craftsmen** from the **Eiffel Tower Company**. The tower was initially built as a **steel structure** for the exposition, and it was intended to showcase the engineering capabilities of the time. However, it was never intended to be a permanent part of the World's Fair and was later **removed** in 1929 and **replaced** by the **Panthéon** in 1930.", '</think>\n\nJimi Hendrix died on **April 27, 1970**, at the age of 24. He was a British guitarist, singer, and songwriter whose innovative use of effects pedals and powerful guitar playing revolutionized the music scene in the 1960s and 1970s. His death was the result of a tragic accident involving a motorcycle and a bus, which occurred during a funeral in the UK.', "</think>\n\nGreat question! Enzymatic shampoo is a type of dog shampoo that's designed to help reduce shedding and maintain the health of your dog's coat. Let me explain it to you:\n\n**Enzymatic shampoo** is a specialized product that contains enzymes, which are proteins that break down dead or damaged hair and dander. These enzymes are effective at removing dead skin cells, shedding, and product buildup from the coat. The enzymes are gentle and safe for all dogs, including puppies and those with sensitive skin.\n\nHere's how it works:\n\n- **Breaks down dead hair** and dander: The enzymes in the shampoo help to loosen and remove dead hair and skin cells, which can contribute to excessive shedding.\n- **Improves coat health**: By removing buildup and debris, enzymatic shampoo can improve the texture and appearance of your dog's coat.\n- **Gentle on the skin**: These shampoos are typically formulated to be gentle and not overly harsh, making them suitable", "</think>\n\nI apologize for the confusion earlier. Let me provide you with a clear and concise list of ingredients needed to make meatballs, which will be covered by the food category. Here's a basic recipe:\n\n**Ingredients:**\n- 2 lbs (about 900g) of ground beef (or a mix of beef and pork for variation)\n- 1 cup (about 200g) of Italian dressing or marinara sauce (for flavor)\n- 1/2 cup (100g) of bread crumbs\n- 1 small onion, finely chopped\n- 1/4 cup (50g) of garlic cloves, minced\n- 1 tsp (5g) of Italian seasoning or herbs (like oregano, thyme, or rosemary)\n- 1 tsp (5g) of salt\n- 1/2 tsp (2g) of black pepper\n- 1 egg (optional, for binding)\n- ", '</think>\n\nAbsolutely! There are many eye makeup products that can help you stand out and enhance your eye features. Here are some key products and tips to consider:\n\n---\n\n### 🤍 **1. Eye Shadow (Eye Palette)**\n- **Best For:** Bold, dramatic, or unique looks.\n- **What to Look For:** A palette with 2–3 colors that can be layered. Look for shades that complement your eye shape and skin tone.\n- **Tips:**\n  - Use a **base color** (lighter than your eye shade).\n  - Use a **mid-color** for the center of your eye.\n  - Use a **dark color** for the outer corner to create a "pop."\n  - Apply with a **blending brush** for a natural look.\n\n---\n\n### 🤍 **2. Eye Liner (Eyeliner)**\n- **Best For:** To define your eye lines, add shape, or make your eyes stand out.\n']
