DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is Kashmir in India or Pakistan?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Do you mean “is Kashmir in India or in Pakistan?”  If so, that question doesn’t have a clear and definite answer.  Kashmir is claimed by both India and Pakistan as their own territory, so each country has “Kashmir” in its name.  To a technical level, both countries have a legal claim to the territory.  There are different issues which complicate this situation, such as human rights and civil rights in Kashmir, the borders of both countries, the effect of the partition of India and Pakistan on Kashmir, etc.  Many people around the world feel that one country has a stronger claim to Kashmir than the other.  Unfortunately, the situation is still in an unclear and unresolved state, and there is no clear path forward.  Each country claims Kashmir as their own.  For this reason, to me, Kashmir is in both India and Pakistan.  If you were asking which country it is most correct to refer to as “Kashmir,” I would suggest that neither is appropriate and we should refer to it as “Kashmir.”'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How is it governed then? Does it have an independent assembly?'}]
