DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'When I cook chicken wings, it hardly retains the flavor. Can you help me figure out why that is?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’d say your suspicion about the flavor is quite correct.  But I think you’re going to need some more information about the problem.  Does it have to do with cooking the wings a certain way, or does it always happen, no matter what you do?  If it’s the former, then maybe the key is something about the way you’re cooking, or maybe something else about the way you cook.  And if it’s the latter, maybe the solution is something about the ingredients or equipment you’re using.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I would say it happens every time I cook,'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'So what happens when you cook?  Is the flavor gone when you put the wings in the oven?  Does the chicken taste good once it’s cooked?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I stick the chicken wings in the oven, and they're marinated. However, when I eat them, they're hardly flavorful. A slight flavor of the marinade is on the,"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Right, so the question I’m seeing is how to use chicken wings so that they’re tastier?  Maybe the marinade is still there when they come out of the oven, but doesn’t have the intensity that you’d want it to.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Exactly, it doesn't have the intensity that I want it to!"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'When you think of intensity, what do you imagine?  Maybe intensity can be related to how much flavor there is, or maybe it’s some other dimension.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How much flavor there is'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Ah, okay.  So you want to preserve the flavor, so you’ll want to either 1) adjust the marinade ingredients, or 2) increase the marinating time.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Maybe increasing the marinating time would help.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yeah, that sounds like the easiest thing to try.  What I’m saying is, the flavor is in the marinade, so we can bring it out and preserve it better by marinating the wings longer.  Just one question, what does the kitchen smell like?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Like slightly chicken'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Do you think it smells good, or just like chicken?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Just like slightly marinated chicken'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'So you’re saying it smells like chicken that’s marinated, but not in a way you want it to.  Let’s come up with some alternative explanations for that.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "We already did. We said I'll marinade it for longer."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'And this is what we agreed on.  But do you see how I tried to bring out your idea of intensity, and now we’re thinking of another idea that can also help us preserve the flavor?  I just thought that was interesting.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, thanks for your help.'}]
