DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Do you have any advice on how to build my credit?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'If you don’t have any history of good credit, getting credit is going to be a hard task.  You’ll have to convince people that you’re credit-worthy.  A few years of debt-free financial behavior will help a lot.  Getting a credit card could also help you build your credit.  Also, keep your credit card balances as low as possible.  Read about the basics of building your credit here: http://bit.ly/build-your-credit-score'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Any other advice on how to build credit. Any tips?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Good credit management is an important step. It’s easy to fall behind on payments, so you should avoid loans whenever possible. In addition to this, also avoid things like predatory lending, like with payday loans.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay thank you for the advice.'}]
