DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you recommend a recipe for a birthday cake?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, here is a recipe:'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Okay, that sounds like a good recipe, but could you go over each step in more detail, I'm a bit confused."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sure!  The first step is to preheat your oven to 400 degrees F.  That means you put the oven on and turn it up to 400 degrees.  The second step is to prepare two cupcake pans by lining them with paper liners and greasing them with butter.  This is because paper liners help prevent the cupcake batter from sticking to the pan.  Then you prepare your cupcake batter by combining 4 eggs, 2 cups of sugar, 4 1/4 cups flour, 2 teaspoons of baking powder, 1 teaspoon of salt, and 1 cup of butter.  After that, you can take the cupcake batter and add it to the cupcake pan, and bake it for about 20 minutes, until the cupcake is done.  Then, to make icing, you mix 1 cup of sugar, 1/2 cup of butter, 1/4 cup of milk, and 1 tablespoon of vanilla extract.  This gives you 1/4 cup of icing, which you can then use to frost the cupcake.  To make 1/4 cup of icing, you can mix 1 cup of sugar, 3/4 cup of butter, 1 egg, and 1 tablespoon of vanilla extract.  This gives you more icing, which you can use to decorate the cupcake.  Voila!  Here’s a picture of your finished cake.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, thanks, I will do that. Could I maybe add something else to the cake mix, such as lemon, or chocolate?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I make chamomile tea?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Here’s how to do that:  First you’ll need to get some dried chamomile flowers.  Chamomile is a type of plant, and a tea can be made from flowers, leaves, or the whole herb.  When you have the plant itself, you can try to make tea by steeping it in boiling water.  Another method is to just steep some chamomile tea leaves in hot water.  The tea will be more concentrated if you let the leaves steep for longer.  Both types of tea will be a bit bitter, and they will taste mostly like chamomile.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'When should I get chamomile flowers from the plant for tea?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'For both types of tea, you’ll need to collect chamomile flowers after the blooms have faded, but before they go brown.  You can store dried chamomile flowers in an airtight container, and you can also use the flowers for other purposes, like making herbal body products.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Thanks for the help with this!'}]
