DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is an LLC? How can I know if I should get one?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'As a general rule, the fewer the rules and regulations governing an organization, the more flexible it is and the more people and organizations that it can bring together. So the term “limited liability corporation” is referring to a business that is designed so that its owners are protected from lawsuits, while at the same time being able to use that same structure to conduct business.  I don’t think you’ll benefit from an LLC in a casual, personal or side business context, since the LLC isn’t really designed for that.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Interesting! What businesses do best as LLCs?'}]
