DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do you keep the paint looking nice on your car?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Oh, that’s a great question! If you look closely, the paint on your car is not a solid material, and you can actually see tiny plastic bubbles. If you left the car in the sun for a day or two, the paint would start to dry out, and the paint particles would shrink, creating the bubbles you see. I also recommend using synthetic wax instead of traditional wax, to keep the paint nice and shiny. What do you think about this approach?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I think that is a great idea. I think I will buy some synthetic wax.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Thank you, I’m so glad I could help!'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is there a special way I should apply it?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is self tanner?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Self-tanner is a product that is applied to your skin to make it darker.  If you want to look as if you are from a tropical area where you spend a lot of time in the sun, or perhaps just from a culture with a darker skin tone, it can be a good option.  It’s a gel, and it goes on your skin just like moisturizer.  You might need to try a few different formulations to find one that works for you.  If you need more help with skin care, let me know.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is it always a gel? Can it look natural?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It’s available in a few different formulas.  Some use powder, some are creamy, others are tinted.  The idea is the same.  If you want to take a look at a review of some of the more common ones, here’s an article you can read: http://www.skininc.com/skinscience/aging/art3767.html'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I can't see the link though."}]
