DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "What's the safest way to pay for a house and lot in cash? Bringing a lot of actual cash with me seems unsafe. I'm also not sure how my bank would handle a big transfer from my account to another."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You can buy property through a real estate agent or a realtor. There are over 1.5 million realtors in the U.S. alone, and many are experienced in working with buyers with cash. In the U.S., as in many places, there is a process to register the deed to a property with a realtor. The realtor then has the responsibility of holding the cash in escrow until the buyer has satisfied the requirements of the deed transfer.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I see. That makes sense. I assume the realtor of course would get something from helping both parties. How much do they usually get, or how much is the fee?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is a secured credit card?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'A secured credit card is one in which you put a deposit in advance to guarantee the use of the card, and then pay back the amount over time, with interest.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'So you have to put money down?'}]
