DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "Hey, I'm wondering how to find free mental health resources? I'd really like to enroll in therapy but it's not in the budget and I don't know where to start"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Yes, it's really a question of need and priority.   Do you think you could just do some light reading on the subject? If you tell me more about what your current situation is like I might be able to point you in a direction."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I have been trying to do more reading and podcasts and journaling, but I think a therapist would be helpful as I am in a position where I have finally left a lifetime abuser'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "There is definitely a lot of ground to cover. There are many free resources available on the web, but it may be difficult to make sense of them.   I think I could help you find what's appropriate and relevant.  I will do this by pairing you with an in-person therapist with expertise in helping you with your particular concerns and goals."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Thanks! How do you pair me with a therapist?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What should I do to survive a shark attack?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’m not an expert on sharks, but if I were you, I’d run in the opposite direction.  They don’t have the best senses, so it might take them a while to realize that you’re there.  Also, sharks are sometimes tempted by strong smells, like blood, and tend to take the first available target.  If you’re careful not to move too fast, you can even turn your back on the shark and walk away slowly, then quickly run when you get a chance.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay I would try to get away if possible. Is there anything else that I can do?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, you can try to stun the shark with something big, like a baseball bat, and jump on its back.  You might also be able to escape by attacking the shark with a sharp, pointy object.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I won't have a baseball bat in the ocean. Hopefully I have something sharp to use. I heard you can also hit a shark in the nose. Does that actually work?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I think it’s unlikely that the shark will let you get close enough to hit it in the nose.  The best defense, again, is to run in the opposite direction, or to take whatever big object you can find and try to stun the shark.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Okay that's good to know."}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What are some methods I can use to help with my social anxiety?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'There are many different kinds of anxiety disorders, and social anxiety is one of them. People can have anxiety for all kinds of situations and situations can change over time.  Are you feeling especially anxious about certain situations, like parties or social gatherings?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I get really anxious during any kind of social gathering.'}]
