DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I deal with a client who is rude and aggressive?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’d suggest it depends on the context. Can you give me some more information about this?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'The client is never polite when he communicates. He demands work that is unpaid. He is impatient. And he makes me uncomfortable.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'So it sounds like you’re getting harassed.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "He isn't quite at the level of harassment, but he sure is offensive. What would harassment look like according the law?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Is he physically intimidating?  Exposing you to bodily harm?  Making crude or explicit sexual remarks?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'No, none of these. What is the legal definition of harassment though?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Well a definition of harassment is something that is calculated to “injure, harm, or annoy someone”, or if someone thinks “that what someone else did could be considered to be harassment.” It also has to “unreasonably interfere with someone's work, work performance, or access to the workplace.”"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Which legal system are you getting this definition from?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The most common definition is U.S. law.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "So if the client is just kind of a rude person, it's not really harassment, is it?"}]
