DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What should I do to treat a jammed finger?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Well, what sort of jammed finger do you mean? There’s a “charley horse” (which is a cramp in a muscle) and a “jammed finger” (where the fingernail sticks into the finger). In either case, one way to remove a stuck fingernail is to grab the nail from the side with tweezers or pliers, and pull it towards you, while also pulling on the skin and nail at the other end. It might be helpful to pull the nail out a little bit, so the whole finger is pulled along with the nail. That should free the nail, and keep you from injuring your finger.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "It's not a cramp and it doesn't have anything to do with a fingernail. A jammed finger is when the end of your finger gets pushed straight back in a forceful way."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Well, sometimes it’s helpful to reduce the pain first, by giving yourself an ice pack or rubbing some ice on the tip of your finger. Once the pain is reduced, you can put more pressure on your finger.   You could push on it very firmly with your hand, for example, or you could push on the other end of the finger.  If you give it a quick hard tap with a hammer, that could help as well.  If that doesn’t work, then you can try to increase the pressure in other ways, like squeezing your finger.  Of course you’ll want to avoid doing any permanent damage to the finger.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "An ice pack sounds good and I will want to stabilize it for now. I definitely don't want to use a hammer like you recommended. That sounds painful."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'This seems like a pretty reasonable plan.  Of course you’ll also want to wear a splint to keep your finger stable and to reduce any movement that might make things worse.  Is there anything else I can help with?  Do you need to think about this a bit?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "That's all for now."}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I'm looking for a new book to read! Can you help?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "I'm glad to help. Are you looking for a certain kind of book? I can recommend some here. You could check out the newest release of the old classic, ‘A Tale of Two Cities’, which is one of the first examples of science fiction! Or maybe you want something closer to home, the most popular romance novel that sold over 1,000 copies? How about a thriller with an unlikely hero?"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What about a good young adult fiction? Do you have any recommendations for that?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Hm, I think I have a few good options for you. The best-selling young adult fiction of 2017 was a ‘superhero’ book, about an abandoned teen who is put into a superhero program and learns the meaning of life. Or if you’re looking for a book about saving the earth, the world, or your career, there’s this classic: ‘Everything I never told you’!'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'That sounds perfect! Thanks!'}]
