DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How can I make my own soap at home?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It’s pretty easy to make your own soap.  Just mix some oils and a few other ingredients together in a pot.  Then it will harden into a bar when it cools.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What kind of oils?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Any oil that is pure and doesn’t include additives will work.  Coconut oil is usually a good choice.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What other ingredients do I need besides oil?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'If you want a hard bar of soap, you’ll want to add a fat like lard or shortening.  You can also add coloring, vitamins, and fragrance for flavor.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What makes the soap harden?'}]
