elps the soap form a solid, rigid bar when it cools.\n\nHere’s what happens during the process:\n\n1. **Oils** (like coconut or palm oil) are liquid when you start the process.\n2. **Fats** (like lard or shortening) are solid and act as a "binders" that help the soap structure.\n3. When you mix the oils and fats together, the fat helps the soap form a firm, solid bar as it cools and solidifies.\n\nSo, the **fat** (lard, shortening, or other animal fats) is what makes the soap hard. Without it, the soap might be more like a liquid or']
