DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please tell me about the former US President Bill Clinton.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '“Bill Clinton (born William Jefferson Blythe III) is an American politician who served as the 42nd President of the United States from 1993 to 2001. Inaugurated at age 46, he was the third-youngest president. He took office at the end of the Cold War, and was the first president since John F. Kennedy to be elected while serving in his first term of office. Clinton was born and raised in Arkansas, and is a Southern Baptist. He played a key role in the Democratic Party during the 1990s as a statesman and leading presidential contender.  He served two terms as Governor of Arkansas. In 1992, Clinton became the first Democrat since Franklin D. Roosevelt to be elected president.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'You said that  the Senate voted to acquit Clinton on both impeachment articles.  Did the majority of Senators at that time belong to the Democratic Party?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes.  The majority of the Senate was composed of Democrats, including 60 of the 67 Senators who voted in favor of acquittal, and 38 of the 45 Senators who voted in favor of conviction.   I don’t know the exact percentages, but Clinton was acquitted by a comfortable margin.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please tell me about the Lewinsky scandal.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '“The Lewinsky scandal was a sex scandal that involved United States President Bill Clinton and White House intern Monica Lewinsky. It led to the impeachment of Clinton by the U.S. House of Representatives on December 19, 1998, and his acquittal by the Senate on February 12, 1999.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Who was Ken Starr?'}]
