DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I have two ribeyes that I want to cook on my charcoal grill.  I've never used a grill before though.  Can you help?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Of course!  This sounds like a great opportunity for us to work together.  In my opinion, it would be really helpful for you to do this, because you can’t really really get the full benefits of using a charcoal grill unless you cook at least one steak on it.  Do you agree?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I agree.  How do I even light a charcoal grill?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I know, I know! That’s the most challenging part of cooking with a charcoal grill!  You’ve got to get the charcoal started somehow, right?  There’s a few tricks we can try, but the easiest way is to just use some lighter fluid.  You’ll want to wait for the charcoal to be a little more thoroughly dried out before you add lighter fluid, because if you add too much lighter fluid too soon it will explode and cover you in burning hot liquid.  Have you ever used lighter fluid before?  It’s actually pretty easy, once you get the hang of it.  Do you want to give it a try?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Ok, I'll use the lighter fluid.  What is the secret to cooking the steaks?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It’s really important to get the heat of the grill up to about 300 F, which is called a medium heat.  If you make it too hot, you’ll cook the steaks too fast and have dry, flavorless steaks.  If you make it too low, then it’ll take forever for the steaks to cook through, and then you’ll have greasy, unappetizing steaks.  What do you think of this plan so far?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'That sounds easy enough.  How long do I cook the steaks on each side?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I'm joining the military and I've heard a lot about something called BUD/S. What is that? It's some sort of training."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "It's the basic training for the United States Navy SEALs, and is the hardest and most demanding military training in the world."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What does it entail?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'A Navy SEAL undergoes a month and a half of training that\'s nearly twice as long as the normal boot camp. During that time the recruits are trained to execute dangerous missions in dangerous environments. The first phase is called "Hell Week" and they train the SEALs to think quickly and work as a team with a common goal.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "BUD/S is the same thing as hell week? I've heard both terms."}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What are some good ice breakers for my students?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Ice breakers are when you’re trying to get your students to feel more comfortable with each other.  It’s a way of helping them to feel welcome in a new setting, and to build community.  Are you saying you’re worried they’ll be scared to speak up and ask questions?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Yeah I think so.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Maybe an icebreaker for a classroom is to talk a bit about your own teaching experience or your current school and tell them some of the things you’ve done to make your classroom welcoming.  You might try describing the ways you’ve started conversations with your students, and then make a point of doing some of that in class to begin a class.  Students may take an extra moment to feel at ease, but I bet that this would help them feel that they can approach you for help.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Sounds good. Anything else?'}]
