DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you tell me the history of Aboriginal Australians?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Great question!  Here is some information about how the Australian continent was settled over the past 60,000 years, and which Indigenous Australians were living here.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Did they come to Australia after or before the British?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'There are a number of accounts and theories about when humans first arrived in Australia, but the most widely accepted is that the earliest humans arrived here over 60,000 years ago.  The story about humans arriving in Australia later is due to the fact that there are no modern humans to compare with Australian Aboriginals.  So the story says that only Indigenous Australians have been here, and so it must have been that the first ones arrived before people moved from Asia to North America.  The story has been disproven by studying genetic data and analyzing the environment in Australia.  If humans were here earlier than 60,000 years, there should be evidence of human activities like villages and settlements.  But there are none.  It was a unique place at the time, with a unique animal community and unique soils.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'You said that the Aboriginals came to Australia 60,000 years ago.  From where?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Well, that’s actually the big question that has yet to be solved!  Here is what we know.  Humans evolved in Africa about 200,000 years ago.  By about 80,000 years ago humans were living throughout Africa.  About 60,000 years ago humans were making tools out of stone.  The only places humans were living at the time were in Asia and Africa, and human populations were growing.  Then, just about 60,000 years ago, humans started settling in places like Europe, and humans were coming into contact with each other in Asia for the first time.  There were no established human cultures at the time, as we know them now.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Do the Aboriginals look like people from Asia or Africa?'}]
