DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What should I look for in a school for my kids?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Do you have a specific school or education philosophy in mind?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I want my children to have the best education possible.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Let’s think about some of the different things you might want from an education for your children.  How about a challenging, but positive environment?  Interesting and helpful information?  Socializing and strong relationships with classmates?  Caring teachers?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I want a challenging, but positive environment for my child to learn.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'What specific challenges do you want your child to face?  How will you know if they’re facing a challenge?  Do you want your child to be tested or evaluated, or should they be able to express their thoughts and feelings?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "When thinking about the right learning institution for my children, I want my child's education to be challenging, but not above their abilities. I would like the teachers to be helpful, patient, and fair with the children at school. I expect examinations to be held periodically throughout the year to ensure the children are learning what has been taught."}]
