DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Kayaking always seem to be such an invigorating sport. How injury-prone, is the sport?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You’re very correct. The number of kayakers who die is far greater than the number of deaths of those who race bikes or swim.  The main risk is the water.  A very small mistake could lead to an accident or a terrible death.  That doesn’t mean that kayakers shouldn’t continue enjoying this sport, but simply that we shouldn’t overestimate their safety.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I've had a few friends, who had a few close calls. What are the ways to make kayaking safer?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "1.  Wear a life jacket and tie it to your kayak.\n2.  Don't use expensive or fragile equipment that can easily break.\n3.  Don't get too much into debt for kayaking equipment.\n4.  Pay close attention to any storm or dangerous weather conditions.\n5.  Always exercise common sense while on the water.\n6.  Wear some personal floatation device."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Those are fantastic suggestions. Especially the life preservers and life jackets.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I know. It can be very difficult to convince someone to wear a life jacket, but believe me, it is the best decision for both their safety and the beauty of kayaking.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'A budget important too. Especially with kayaking. Easy to spend a lot.'}]
