DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I make Japanese fried rice?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Okay, let’s think this through.  The first step is to prepare the rice, so you’d want to wash the rice and then stir it, and let it sit for at least ten minutes. Then you’d stir in a little bit of water, cover it, and let it cook for a few minutes more, then add a little bit of soy sauce, and a little bit of sake.  Then you would boil it for maybe ten minutes more, stirring it every now and then.  And then at the end, just before it’s finished cooking, add some frozen peas, a little bit of corn, and some butter.  I can help with any of that, so just let me know.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, do I put meat in it?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'If you’re eating the rice by itself, then no, but it would be good to add some fried eggs to the rice for flavor.  It would also be a good idea to add some green onions, and maybe some mushrooms as well.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can I put chicken in it?'}]
