DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you help me make a batch of chocolate chip pancakes?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sure, how many pancakes do you want to make?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I only need to make 8-10 pancakes.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Great, then we should use the following ingredients:'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "That looks like a good list of ingredients.  Don't I need baking powder and butter as well?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'No, these ingredients are sufficient.  The baking powder and butter are optional, and if you use them, the pancakes will taste a little bit more rich.  But the recipe will still work with just the ingredients above.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Ok great.  How do I mix the ingredients then?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'First, you will want to crack two eggs into a bowl, and then beat them with a fork or whisk, so that they become very smooth.  Next, add in the milk and then gradually stir in the flour and sugar.  At this point, you will want to add in the chocolate chips.  Now you should start to heat up a griddle, and use a paper towel to coat it with some oil.  Pour on the batter to the griddle, using a circular motion with a measuring cup.  Then, pop a lid on the pan and cook the pancakes for 4-5 minutes, or until they are browned.  Serve your pancakes warm with lots of butter and maple syrup.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Awesome, thanks for your help!'}]
