DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How can I improve my basketball shooting accuracy?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'This depends on a number of factors, such as your current skill level, your fitness, and also whether you are trying to be an accurate jump shooter or a highly accurate off the dribble shooter. I can help you to improve either skill.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'For now I want to focus on my jump shot.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The key to any basketball shot is to release the ball as close as possible to the peak of your jump. As a result, we will focus on improving your body mechanics and ability to generate power from your legs when you jump. To maximize your power in this way, you will need to make sure you land on the balls of your feet and bend your knees as you touch the ground. A picture is worth a thousand words, so please take a look at the video and the instructions that follow it.  If you have questions or would like to move on to the next set of video exercises, just tell me.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay so the shot starts in the legs and then I also need good form when using my arms to shoot the ball.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'That’s right, it starts in the legs.  As you’re jumping, do everything you can to try and keep your hips level, and also to avoid pulling your head forward.  Your shoulders should be relaxed, and you should be looking down the court, towards the hoop.  As you’re jumping you should also squeeze the ball as tight as possible with both hands.  When you’re in the air, aim for a place where you can make contact with the ground at the peak of your jump.  If you land on your toes your feet will be in a low position, and you’ll have a better chance of shooting accurately.  On the other hand, if you land flat on your feet, then you’ll want to pivot your body to prepare to jump again.   In this video I’ll demonstrate these techniques:'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Thanks. I was able to learn a lot in a short amount of time from talking with you.'}]
