DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I'm sensitive to WiFi. How can I protect myself from the WiFis from the neighbors? I live in an apartment."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "As you probably know, WiFi is wireless communication technology. It's something like how an electrical outlet lets you connect electrical devices. You can make your apartment look more like an electrical outlet by placing your router inside of a closet. The closet will block outside signals coming in through the walls of the apartment. You can also buy a signal-blocking device, but you may have to sign a service agreement. The service agreement will allow the wireless companies to send you information about their services. They might also want you to tell them how you are using their services."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I'm asking you how to shield myself from my neighbor's WiFi signal."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I don\'t know what the "neighbor" in this situation refers to, or where exactly the WiFi signal is coming from.  A WiFi signal travels through the air, so the strongest signal can be located by how high up it is, and how far away it is.  I\'m happy to help you decide whether to shield yourself from your neighbors WiFi, if you can give me more information.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'There are neighbors downstairs, upstairs, and next door with WiFi routers. I can see them from my computer. How can I shield myself? Can I put something on the walls?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Are you saying that you are on the same floor as the neighbors with the routers?  Are you planning to place a block of some kind on the walls between you and them? Or maybe you want to learn more about the WiFi networks they are using?  I could explain to you what a WiFi router looks like, or how to view someone's WiFi signal strength."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I already know I want to shield myself, and I can see how strong they are by how many bars show up.'}]
