DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How can I raise butterflies?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'If you don’t want to raise a lot of different species, you might be able to start with a butterfly garden that only has a few different species.  These plants will attract butterflies and support them while they’re present.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What plants attract the most butterflies?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Flowers with a lot of different colors in them are very attractive to butterflies.  A lot of common flowers like dandelions, clover, and sunflowers.  If you don’t have a lot of sunshine, you can also try trying plants that can grow in part shade like daffodils.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I didn't know butterflies liked sunflowers."}]
