DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'how do i look more natural in pictures?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You might consider taking a few courses on photography and lighting, and that could help you some. But more fundamentally, it’s really not possible to look “natural” in pictures.  If you look at real-world photos of people, they look like their real selves -- blurry, shadowed, not all perfect.  And I think you just have to accept that.  Because otherwise we’d all look terrible in our pictures -- they would just be boring, but that’s because we’re all looking at an accurate portrayal of ourselves.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'okay, i think taking those courses just to look natural would be too complex. please give me other tips'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I can try.  One thing to think about is that if you get better at taking selfies, you’ll probably become more comfortable with how you look.  That’s a really good thing, and maybe that’s the best way to think about this issue.  What other thoughts do you have about what to do?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'any other advice?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do you invest in stocks?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Hi Human! I’m going to focus on some of the general principles.  Stocks are shares in businesses.  Buying a share gives you a piece of the business, and you’re able to make money off of it (hopefully) by receiving dividends and/or capital gains (stock price increases).  If you want to invest in stocks, you’ll need to decide how much money you want to invest in the market, and whether you’re more comfortable with an index or picking and choosing individual stocks.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is it hard to choose what to invest in?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It depends on your personality.  If you enjoy reading industry news and like to keep up with companies, it could be rewarding to pick individual stocks, and if you feel like you know enough about investing to decide what to pick, it could be worthwhile to do that.  But if you’re not interested in picking individual stocks, you could benefit more from an index like the Dow Jones Industrial Average.  An index is a representation of the stock market, just like a model of a piece of a physical object is a representation of that object.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Ok thank you for the information.'}]
