DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I avoid carpal tunnel?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You need to stop typing for a while, and if you can see your keyboard while you’re typing, that’s a bad sign.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What if my job is to type all day?  How do I prevent carpal tunnel then?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You don’t want to do that.  Most carpal tunnel comes from typewriter use and repetitive motions, and while you may need to type on a computer for your job, you should at least take breaks.  To get some advice about where and how to take breaks, you could ask people who know you well.  Here are some guidelines from an article I found, “How Much Time Between Typing Sequences?”, which say, “A comfortable pause between typing sequences is four minutes, but it’s not just duration that’s important. It’s also the volume of work completed between breaks that counts.”'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Do you have an exercises to recommend to prevent carpal tunnel?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Your muscles will naturally strengthen over time as you’re typing, but if you want to make your muscles stronger faster, the article says, “another way to get stronger hands is to do strengthening exercises or build up your hand muscles”. The article suggests pushing weights in a vertical direction and suggests doing these exercises at least three times a week for two weeks.  Once you’ve built up those muscles, you’ll likely want to continue doing them, but of course you don’t want to overdo it.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Thanks for the help!'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Do the railroads still own all the land the Government gave them to build the rails across America?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Oh, I’m afraid the original government gave them about 150,000 square miles.  Today there are only about 1,800 square miles remaining in the hands of the railroads.  This land is mostly used to support industries and supply facilities for the railroad.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'That is crazy! Imagine what that would be worth today!'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'I love hot dogs but I always hear horror stories about what kind of strange ingredients are put into hot dogs. What exactly are hot dogs made of?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The primary ingredients are actually meat and fat, with many variations possible.  On average, a hot dog is around 70 percent lean meat, 20 percent fat, and 10 percent water, but this can vary depending on the specific recipe, and as you’ve noticed the exact ingredients do vary between brands and markets.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'But what about the horror stories of all sorts of odds and ends of animals being mashed into hot dogs and then sold? What parts of animals typically make up hot dogs?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'In the US, hot dogs typically only contain the meat and fat of the dog itself.  But you are correct that a number of other kinds of animals are eaten, and the most commonly consumed parts of an animal end up in hot dogs, which are as follows:'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Are these parts unhealthy, or are they still edible?'}]
