DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'I want to be more productive at work but I have trouble staying motivated, do you have any advice for me?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'One idea is to try measuring your daily progress, so you can keep a check on how well you’re doing.  There are a couple ways you could do this, but maybe the best thing is to keep a kind of notebook where you write down what you expect to get done, and then mark off what you actually did.  This way you can stay aware of what’s going on in your day, and make sure you’re acting on what you want to do and focusing your time on your priorities.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay and how else can I stay motivated?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'This is actually a very challenging question for many people, so what I can try to do here is brainstorm with you a little, and you can tell me which ideas you like, and which don’t.  \nOne idea might be to set aside a specific time to start each day’s tasks, but another idea might be to simply work constantly on whatever’s in front of you.  Do you work with other people, or do you have direct control over your workload and it’s predictable?  Sometimes this can affect how easy it is to stay focused and motivated, or it can be really distracting to work with others.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I work alone at the moment'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'What else could you do to make sure you’re getting the most out of your time?  Maybe there are ways to change your environment that would help you stay motivated and focus?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Such as?'}]
