rpose flour\n- 1½ cups (300g) cold butter (cut into small pieces)\n- 2 ½ cups (300g) sugar\n- 1 tsp salt\n- 1 tsp vanilla extract\n- 1½ cups (300ml) buttermilk or sour cream (optional, for extra richness)\n\n**For the filling:**\n- 2 ½ cups (600g) frozen key lime pie mix (or 1½ cups fresh limes + 1½ cups lime juice)\n- ½ cup (1', '<think>\n\n</think>\n\nYes, APIs can be secure, but they require careful design and implementation to prevent security threats like unauthorized access, data breaches, and misuse.\n\n### How to Make APIs Secure:\n\n1. **Authentication**  \n   - Use **tokens** (like OAuth2 or JWT) to authenticate users or applications.\n   - Require **secure communication** (HTTPS) to protect data in transit.\n\n2. **Authorization**  \n   - Implement rules to ensure only authorized users or systems can access certain endpoints.\n   - Use role-based access control (RBAC) or similar models.\n\n3. **Input Validation**  \n   - Validate all inputs to prevent injection attacks (e.g., SQL injection, command injection).\n   - Sanitize data to avoid malicious payloads.\n\n4. **Rate Limiting**  \n   - Prevent abuse by limiting the number of requests a single user or IP can make per second.\n\n5. **CORS (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing)**  \n   - Restrict which domains can', '</think>\n\nBeer is made by taking a grain, usually barley, and boiling it with water, then adding hops, and then letting it ferment.  The grain is milled to make a fine powder, which is then mixed with hot water and sometimes some other ingredients.  The mixture is then allowed to ferment, which is a process where the yeast helps the beer to become drinkable.  The fermentation process is crucial to the flavor and overall character of the beer.', '</think>\n\nThat\'s a great question! It\'s interesting that you\'re thinking about how cats evolved to communicate with humans, especially since you\'re aware of the research that suggests meowing might be part of their communication with people. Let me 