paces (like your desk or home), and build from there.\n\n**3. Use Tools**  \nLaptops, notebooks, digital calendars, and apps (like Google Tasks or Trello) can help manage tasks and schedules.\n\n**4. Prioritize**  \nUse the "Eisenhower Matrix" to prioritize tasks based on urgency and importance.\n\n**5. Batch Similar Tasks**  \nGroup similar tasks (e.g., paying bills, washing dishes) to reduce the time needed and prevent interruptions.\n\n**6. Set Boundaries**  \nLearn to say no, set aside time for rest and hobbies, and avoid overcommitting.\n\n**7']
