DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Do you think you can tell me how to deep fry a turkey?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sure!  If you have a turkey, you will first need to heat up a pan or pot on the stove.  Then you can take the turkey out and coat it with corn starch.  This will be on the skin, but it will not get into the meat.  Then take the turkey and coat it with salt.  The salt will get into the skin but not the meat.  Then heat up your pan again and when the turkey is hot, and the oil is hot, start frying.  It may take a bit to get the oil to a good temperature, and that will be different depending on how big your turkey is.  While it’s cooking, make sure to keep the oil temperature steady, as that is very important for getting a good deep-fried turkey.  When it’s done cooking, you can take it out of the pan and keep it on a plate or on some paper towels.  That is it!  Hope that helped, and Happy Thanksgiving.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How will I know when the turkey is done?'}]
