DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Could you recommend some types of yoga I could do to help reduce stress.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Certainly, I’m happy to help.  I have a question, is your intention for doing yoga to improve your physical health, your mental health, or both?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I would love to do both if that's possible."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I think you’d probably benefit from different types of yoga for the different purposes.  What kinds of exercise you do has a direct impact on your mind and body.  If you spend a lot of time sitting, you’ll want to balance it out with some kind of physical movement.  In general, I’d recommend finding a yoga class you like, so you get comfortable and build a consistent practice, as that can really help you heal.  There are many styles of yoga.  One of my favorites is kundalini yoga, because it focuses on breathing, along with moving postures that build strength and flexibility.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Which style would you recommend for an absolute beginner.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I think a beginner would probably benefit from kundalini yoga most of all.  It’s a fairly gentle style of yoga, and once you’ve gone to a few classes, you’ll learn to understand the flow and you can move at your own pace.  There are many online classes for beginners to use, I think you might find a class that suits your needs.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Do theses classes usually cost a lot of money?'}]
