DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "Why do people get tattoo's?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Tattoo's are body modifications and used by many cultures to display one's interests and values.  In the United States many of those who choose to get a tattoo may have a value of being a bad-ass, or a particular religious affiliation.  Would you like to get a tattoo?"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'No not really. I just wonder why so many people seem to be showing them off?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "I am sorry you are not interested in getting a tattoo, but I see your curiosity about people having tattoos.  It is a common way to visually show off a particular culture, and can even be used to indicate ownership or as a means of status identification.  Many people choose to cover up their tattoo's or turn them into a tattoo that appears to be natural.  I’ve seen people in bathing suits or people dressed for work that seem to have covered up tattoo's in this way.  Some people also might choose to remove a tattoo that they regret, or that has negative connotations, such as if it can be associated with illegal activities.  Have you ever seen someone who had a tattoo on their face that was very clearly not what the person intended to have on their face?"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Yes it seemed that way.'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please tell me places to visit in New York City.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Here are some suggestions:  I highly recommend checking out the Statue of Liberty.  You can also go to Central Park and take a ride on the Carousel.  Maybe see a show at Radio City Music Hall?  You can also find the famous museum called the Museum of Natural History, or go to the city’s planetarium.  Here are also some lesser-known things to do, like see the Tompkins Square Park Hip-Hop Fountain, or ride the High Line elevated park on the former elevated railway.  This park is a super interesting way to get a great view of the city, as well as some stunning architectural features like the Bellevue and The Lillian Wald Houses.  You can also do some really cool things with food, like check out some “Sky Rides” on the High Line, or get a 360-degree view of the city with the Hudson River Skateway.  There are also many cool restaurants to check out, like the Williamsburg Marketplace, and you can’t miss the Barclays Center, where the New York Knicks play!'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I heard if you go in winter, you can ice skate at Rockefeller Center.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Here are some suggestions:   Ice skating at Rockefeller Center is indeed fun, but there are so many more wonderful ice skating places to visit!  There is an awesome ice skating rink in Central Park that’s free to skate on, and it’s a great way to see the park in the winter.   You can also check out the Rockefeller Plaza ice rink that’s part of the Empire State Building complex, and there are so many great outdoor skating rinks in winter, like the Washington Square Park Ice Skating Rink.   I’d also recommend the West Side Skating Rink, that’s built on the roof of the first train station to run on Manhattan.  But, if you want to go somewhere a bit more isolated from the hustle and bustle, you should definitely check out the Rockaway Beach Ice Rink, and enjoy the scenic ocean views, while you ice skate!'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is Rockefeller Center far away from the Time Square?'}]
