DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do you make a safe and sturdy wood pizza oven?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'For starters, you’ll probably want to make sure that the pizza oven is in the correct condition to be operated.  This will help to minimize the likelihood that someone gets hurt while you’re making pizza.  Also, pizza is one of the most popular pizzas in America, so there’s a high likelihood that someone’s going to want to make a pizza oven someday.  With that in mind, you can think about preparing yourself to make an awesome oven.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I have some space in my patio out near my grill that I thing would be perfect to have a pizza oven built on but I want to make sure I do it right.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'We’ve already discussed the importance of the initial conditions for operating the pizza oven, and you’ve said you’re going to build on the patio near your grill.  It sounds like your priority is to make the best pizza oven you can.  This is great, I love pizza too!'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'yes wood oven pizza is delicious and it also helps prevent you warming up your house when cooking a pizza.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I totally agree that wood-fired pizza is delicious!  Did you have any specific questions about the process of building a pizza oven?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'not specific questions more of general ones like what type of brick, how much cement and what shape or design?'}]
