DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'I really liked Interstellar. What other movies or tv shows like it do you recommend?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The film is really well-done, and the visuals are breathtaking. But I want to make sure I give you an appropriately wide selection of recommendations. First off, if you’re like me and think it was great but you really wished there was more exploration of space-related topics, I’d recommend Contact, Apollo 13, Moon, and Gravity.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Those are good recommendations, but I'm looking for something that explores more on space stuff - whether fictional or not - like blackholes, wormholes, humans finding a new earth, etc."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'This is a tough request because there really isn’t a lot of speculative fiction that covers those topics.  I can see why the Interstellar movie does a good job of exploring space, and it seems like you’re looking for something more specifically focused on the various possibilities and difficulties of interstellar travel. I don’t think this is a shortcoming of Interstellar specifically, but I think the problem here is that “near-future space travel” is not that interesting of a science fiction topic.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Ah, that - interstellar or interplanetary travel (like that more recent movie about Mars with the Bourne trilogy actor). I have to disagree with you though. I think near-future space travel is a pretty interesting sci-fi topic. So, any recommendations?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’m not sure I can really say what I think of Interstellar as being a valid movie about space-travel, when it focuses on some non-obvious and definitely untrue ideas. I mean, it’s definitely a good movie, but I wouldn’t have expected you to like it if you had a real interest in space travel. Maybe The Martian is more what you’re looking for?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "But it is also from 2011, so it won't really have the near future feel you're looking for.  Maybe another movie that came out in 2015, like Passengers or The Martian?"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Sorry, I mispoken. I wanted to say I already watched The Martian. Also, Passengers. Any other recommendations?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Okay, so I was thinking about Interstellar, and I know I’ve heard of a movie or two that might be similar to what you’re looking for.  I could look up a description, but I’m not sure what’s out there.  Can you describe a bit more what kind of “near-future space travel” scenario you’re interested in?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Something like the sun or the earth dying, or humans colonizing other planets, systems or stars.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Do you mean humans creating new, or alternative, planets and habitats?  Or actual space travel?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Both I guess.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I think there’s a movie called Passengers, which is about “colonizing” another planet (similar to Interstellar) but might be a bit different, since it focuses more on human relationships and decisions, rather than action and exploration.  Maybe you would enjoy it?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Thanks, I've seen it already and does like it too. I'm just thinking there might be another movie or tv show out there I've missed in the past few years."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Okay, there’s a popular science fiction TV series called The Expanse that might be good for you.  I could give you some more information about the plot if you’d like?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Sure, just no spoilers.'}]
