DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How does a space heater work?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'A space heater is a device that generates heat for humans to use, to keep warm.  Space heaters are used inside a house or other structures, but they are also used outdoors on camping trips or at other outdoor places like hiking trails.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do they work from a technical standpoint?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'A space heater contains an electric heating element, which converts electrical energy into heat.  Most space heaters have an electric cord that connects to an electric outlet in a building, and some space heaters have a propane gas tank that provides fuel for combustion.  If you look inside a space heater, you’ll see a mechanism that keeps the electrical heating element powered up even when the heating element isn’t being directly heated.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'okay thanks'}]
