DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How can I get my clothes to come out of the wash smelling and looking super clean?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'That’s a tough one. Let’s talk through it, shall we? I think there are a few different things we could focus on here.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Does the type of laundry soap I am using affect the cleanliness of the clothing I wash?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’ve read that detergents can vary quite a bit in how clean they are. I’m curious, do you know which laundry detergent you are using? Do you have a specific brand or store you get it from? Can you describe your process of washing clothing? Maybe you could show me the package and list ingredients, or describe the process you use when washing your clothing.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I begin by separating the colored clothing from the white clothing. I usually presoak white clothes in bleach and soak extra dirty things, like socks, in detergent for roughly thirty minutes before placing the clothes in the washing machine. For t-shirts with sleeves, I scrub the underarm area with a bar of soap to remove sweat stains and then toss those in the wash too.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’m not sure I’d ever trust a bar of soap to remove stains from clothing. Can you tell me more about what sort of stains are hard to remove? What sort of cleaning products do you use? I see that you’ve used household bleach to clean your clothes, can you tell me more about that? \nDo you wash your clothes in hot or cold water?\nWhat is the temperature that your clothes are exposed to during washing?\nDo you ever use fabric softener on your clothing?\nHow do you dry your clothing after washing?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I do not have a certain type of soap that I use to wash my clothes. I usually buy the washer soap that is available when I buy groceries.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Are there any brands you prefer?'}, {'role': 'user',