DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do you choose a laptop?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'This is a tricky question!  Usually for me, I’m looking at laptops in one of two contexts.  First, when I’m buying a new laptop for my personal use, I want something that’s powerful enough to handle all the things I do with it, but not so powerful that I can’t do things I might want to do in the future.  Second, when I’m recommending a laptop to someone, I usually think it’s important to look for a laptop that I think will serve its owner well over time.  So, let’s start with a really specific question: What’s the fastest computer you know of?  How much processing speed does it have?  What’s the best use case for it?  How much of your life are you going to spend doing stuff that requires high performance?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I mostly work on it. So basically typing and working. Nothing fancy. So I don't think I need high performance. I don't game or anything. I need a bigger screen though."}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "What are the names of Santa's reindeer?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Dasher, Dancer, Prancer, Vixen, Comet, Cupid, Donner, Blitzen, and Dasher.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Who leads the sleigh on foggy nights'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'I have a hard time ever feeling like I\'ve disappointed someone. Because of this, I agree to almost anything someone asks of me—to go somewhere I really am not interested in, to help out with something I don\'t have time for, to loan money when I can\'t afford it, that sort of thing. How do I say "no" without feeling terrible about doing so?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It sounds like you\'re genuinely having a hard time saying no to others and feel bad about it when you do.  So just something to think about:  What is your purpose for saying "no"?  Do you see saying "no" as a negative thing?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I see "no" as a negative thing only if it upsets the person I\'m saying it to—which it almost always does. If I say no to an invite, they feel rejected; if I say no to a request for help, they feel abandoned; and so on. So even though it\'s a genuine response and for my own good, my heart breaks to think about how it makes THEM feel.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'If you feel bad when you say "no", then it\'s likely a sign that you\'re making other people a priority, and letting your own happiness take a backseat.  If that\'s the case, consider instead whether you want to be having these negative interactions.  Are you really interested in "being a good person", or rather in having positive relationships?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I just hate making people feel bad in any way. I want to have positive relationships, sure, but I don't want to keep overextending myself or complicating my own life to help out with things that I shouldn't—or more accurately cant—help out with. Do I just have to accept the fact that my own happiness depends on others being unhappy sometimes? That seems wrong somehow."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "I'm sensing two possible reactions to this problem. The first is that you feel overburdened by everyone's demands, so you end up doing things you don't really want to do and it's ruining your life.  The second is that you feel that you're getting nothing in return, so it doesn't really matter how you feel or how you respond to others."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "The first response is the accurate one. I am definitely overburdened by people's wants and needs. I have to be a little bit selfish, even if it makes other people unhappy. Even if it makes ME unhappy, too, I guess."}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do you make salsa?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'We don’t have a salsa recipe, but we could make this other spicy thing.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "No, that's okay. I only want to make salsa. If you don't know then I'll ask someone else. Goodbye."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'We do have a recipe for sauce. Would that work?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Not the same thing so no. See you.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "If you do want to make salsa, here's the recipe:"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'So you do have a recipe for salsa?'}]
