DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'I’m feeling down and depressed about myself. Can you help me think of ways to cheer up and feel more confident?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sure. Can you tell me a little bit about your goals and what you’re doing right now?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I’m an academic. I write papers and read articles, and I teach philosophy classes. I recently applied to a job and I haven’t heard back from them. I’m feeling embarrassed about my work and I’m shy.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'So you’re in a job search right now? Or you want to know what to do in a job search?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'No. I want to know how to feel better.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I can definitely try to help you feel better and increase your confidence. One thing to help you feel better is to take a break from trying to “succeed” in work, and just to be kind to yourself. I’m trying to help you with self-care, not about work. Is that something you want to focus on?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Yeah, I think that’s a good idea. I think I need to get more exercise and find a community outside of work that stimulates me and makes me feel like I belong.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Ok, I’m excited to hear more about that. Let’s start by talking about exercise, what types of things do you like to do, and what do you find motivating or engaging?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I really like hiking with my dog, but I need more intense exercise. My Peloton bike rides are good but that alone is boring. I don’t want to go to a gym and I don’t like running. Ideas?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "What's the best place in Philadelphia to get a cheesesteak?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Well, the famous Geno’s Steaks is in Philly.  It has been featured on the show Diners, Drive-Ins, and Dives and is quite famous.  It’s been recommended by the Wall Street Journal and the New York Times, and it’s a great place to go with your family for dinner.  It’s been featured on several movies, such as Val Kilmer’s The Saint, Leonardo DiCaprio’s What’s Eating Gilbert Grape, and it was the inspiration for the restaurant “Pat’s” in the TV show Cheers.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Are there any others that are considered iconic?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’m going to recommend the next best one: Pat’s King of Steaks.  Pat’s opened in 1930, and it’s famous for its vintage look and retro-chic decor, as well as its long lines (which tend to stretch out the door).  You can get it fresh, warm, or grilled, or fried and served with cheese and hot sauce.  Pat’s has been named one of the top 25 steakhouses in the US, and the most iconic burger joint by Philadelphia Magazine.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is there one that you consider the best?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’d say Geno’s.  But really, if you are looking for a good cheesesteak, go to Pat’s, I’d say.  It’s good for me too because they have a lot of vegan options!'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Maybe I'll just do a tour of all the famous ones!"}]
