DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do you heat up leftover fish?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'There are several ways, but one common approach is to put the fish in a saucepan and then cover it with hot water and allow it to cook.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, great. Any other ideas?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You can also use a microwave, which is easy, fast, and relatively cheap.  You just need to remove the skin and any bones from the fish, cut it into pieces, then put it in a microwavable dish with a bit of water and cover it with a microwaveable plate.  Then heat it for three minutes or so on full power, stirring occasionally.  It’s good to use a plate so you can hold the heat longer.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'All right, that makes sense.'}]
