DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I decide between getting a cat or a dog?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’m curious about this as well, how did you come to this choice?  Do you just like one more than the other, or have you tried both and decided that one is better for you?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I haven't yet."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Would you be interested in discussing your criteria for what would make you decide between getting a cat or a dog?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Yes'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Do you prefer to have a pet that you can take outside?  Or do you want a pet that can stay inside the house?  What about the pet’s size, is this important?  If your life is really busy, do you care if your pet will require quite a lot of your time?  Or is it more important to have a pet that will play with you on occasion?  Or will you just want a pet to share the couch with?  Or perhaps you don’t care about any of those details?  I wonder if you want a pet with a distinct personality, or whether you are more interested in getting a pet that just does whatever you'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I guess I prefer an inside pet'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Hmm. So your criteria seem to be that you want an inside pet, or a pet that will play with you on occasion, or a pet that will just be good company.  Is that correct?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Sure'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Okay, so to help me understand, which of these things are most important for you?  Is it just having a pet that you enjoy hanging out with, or is it more important for the pet to be low maintenance, or for the pet to have a special personality?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'low maintenance is good'}]
