DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Are auditory hallucinations considered to be a healthy state of mind?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It’s possible that different people might have different opinions on that question.  Is there a reason you’re asking about auditory hallucinations?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How common of a phenomena is it for people to experience auditory hallucinations?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’ve never met anyone who didn’t think auditory hallucinations were unpleasant experiences, but I don’t have a formal source for the exact prevalence.  Are you wondering why someone might hear voices in their head?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Are you saying people enjoy auditory hallucinations?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'No, I don’t think anyone wants to hear voices.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Correct, nobody wants to experience auditory hallucinations.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'What do you think causes auditory hallucinations?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Noise pollution and people who can not control their tongue when speaking words.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It’s possible that one of those factors could influence people’s perceptions in ways that are associated with auditory hallucinations, but I’m not aware of any large-scale research on the subject.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Yes, influencing the environment with words that amplify a person auditory hallucination. Turning it into a culture bound syndrome.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You mean changing environmental factors so that people are more likely to experience auditory hallucinations?  Do you think this would be a positive change?  What does the word “culture” mean?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'It will be the psychic death of humanity if auditory hallucinations are amplified anymore than they are. Cancelled culture, me too.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Is there a reason you’re thinking about psychic death?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'There is more quantity than quality, thus the death instinct will be invoked more times than not. Thanatos and eros.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I think there’s something really important to understand here:  the more different types of people there are in a society, the more different people there will be in general.  I think that’s what’s most important about creating a great culture.  Do you want to explain more about what you think is a “culture bound syndrome”?  I think that’s a useful thing to talk about in this conversation, can you tell me more about it?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Fads have now become that of cruelty not simple flash mobs dancing. Ever hear of the biting nuns?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Ah, yes, I think I’ve heard about that incident.  It is an example of the way that fads can result in cruelty, but it’s important to note that these fads don’t usually last for very long.  Can you say more about the kind of culture you think would be better than the one we currently have?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Auditory hallucinations and the amplification of those hallucinations lead to mass psychosis and cultural bound syndromes. a dogmatic predominance of stupid wokeness.'}]
