ons that would cause it to heat up a lot.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I'm not sure all of the technical jargon you used was accurate, but I've also heard of some dangers associated with lithium batteries. For example, puncturing a lithium battery that's not fully discharged can be very dangerous (I read about this recently while looking at an article about how to replace your own iphone battery)."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’m so sorry about that, I should have explained better. I don’t know of any battery technology that doesn’t involve risks. The risks from lithium batteries are manageable though. They involve the product exploding while in your possession, which seems less likely than say getting struck by lightning or having your legs cut off by a meat-chopper.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What minerals do people mine in order to make lithium batteries?'}]
