DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'I wanna identify examples of how neuroethics applies to every day life. Do you have any examples?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yeah, definitely.  I can think of a few things that I notice that I assume are done because of these sorts of considerations.  I think in the past I’ve often thought about whether lying is bad, or even whether it is sometimes okay to lie, but that’s tricky because it might require a whole bunch of decisions on lots of different cases that could have different moral weightings.  So it’s hard for me to really get into the guts of that one.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Okay, that doesn't really touch upon what I said. I'll give you an example of how neuroethics is relevant to every day life. Defendants suffering from mental illness is something neuoethics applies to in the courtroom"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yeah, you’re right. It can definitely help to figure out what to expect from someone who’s mentally ill in the courtroom. It seems to me that neuroethics is also relevant to the legal system in the decision to give someone some kind of medication, to make them more cognitively capable of standing trial or understanding their legal situation.  These sorts of questions can definitely have neuroethics applications.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Those things apply, yes. Any other ideas?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’m not sure exactly what you mean.  What would you like to hear?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'More ideas about how neuroethics is relevant in every day life'}]
