DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'how can i get my kids to wake up for school?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’m happy to help.  It sounds like the problem is you want to wake up your kids early so that they’re ready for school.  Does that sound right?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Right.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Well, it sounds like they’ve been having trouble waking up.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'They have.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'There are a couple of different things we could do:  First, we could increase the time before their alarms.  Maybe waking up an hour later each day would help, until they are waking up on time, when we gradually decrease the time.  The other approach would be to increase their total sleep time so they wake up later.  For example, maybe we could increase the amount of sleep they get each night, so they wake up a little later in the morning.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "wouldn't an hour later be opposite?"}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I've heard a lot about cell phones causing cancer or brain tumors with their signals. Is there any scientific evidence for this?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Cell phones do emit RF radiation, which is electromagnetic radiation that can cause the body to absorb and emit energy. The long-term health effects of electromagnetic fields have not been well studied, but the American Cancer Society’s website says the American Cancer Society does not have sufficient scientific evidence to determine if cell phones cause cancer. If you do wish to lower your cell phone’s radiofrequency exposure, we recommend that you carry your phone in a cell phone case. We do recommend that you avoid holding the phone close to your body while it is on, as some people claim that these practices may be connected to specific health concerns. We recommend being mindful of the location of cell towers to minimize long-term exposure to RF radiation, though we do not have any scientific evidence to suggest this is necessary.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How far away should I hold phones from my body to be safe?'}]
