DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you tell me how a pension is used for retirement planning?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Pensions are one of the most popular tools for retirement planning, even though a few people find them outdated or confusing.  Pensions are a way to make money, and people pay for them.  In a basic sense, you can think of a pension as paying someone to work for you, when you’re not working.  So let me give you an example:  If you work in a company, and earn a regular paycheck, and then your company also gives you a pension that lets you keep earning money in retirement, then it is as if you get to work'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Okay thanks. How does someone's pension get funded?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You can have a pension that’s funded by government or company, or sometimes by you and your company, or you and your family.  Depending on what kind of pension you choose, and how much you choose to pay for it, it will get funded differently.  A pension that’s funded by the government means that a percentage of your paycheck is going into a government pension plan.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Alright, and can you tell me how the person receives their pension?'}]
