he growth is added to your pension.\n- **How you receive it**:\n  - You receive a **defined benefit** pension, which is usually paid in a structured way, such as a monthly payment or a lump sum.\n  -", '</think>\n\nOkay, let me clarify this. When I mentioned baking, I was referring to the general cooking method—like baking in the oven, but I might have been using the term loosely. However, when it comes to Kung Pao chicken, a common and traditional preparation involves frying the ingredients, especially the chicken and the peanuts, in a pan.\n\nSo, to make Kung Pao chicken properly, you would typically:\n\n1. **Fry the peanuts** until they are golden and crisp.\n2. **Fry the chicken** in a pan, adding some oil and seasonings like soy sauce, chili paste, and garlic.\n3. **Combine everything** in a bowl, then **fry it all together** in the pan, adding more seasonings and some water or broth if needed.\n4. **Bake** it in the oven for a few minutes, but this is more of a quick method, as the dish is often served quickly.\n\nSo, the key', '</think>\n\nThat’s a great question! If the crack is **small** and **not too deep**, you can indeed **fill it with concrete** and let it set. Here are the **simple steps** to repair a small crack in gray concrete:\n\n---\n\n### **Step-by-Step Guide to Repairing a Small Crack in Gray Concrete**\n\n#### **1. Clean the Crack**\n- **Wet the area** with a damp cloth to remove dust, dirt, or debris.\n- Use a **brush** or **small brush** to clean the crack thoroughly.\n- Make sure the crack is **dry and free of any residue**.\n\n#### **2. Prepare the Concrete**\n- If the crack is **not deep** (e.g., just a minor split or a very small crack), you can **skip** the grout or filler.\n- If the crack is **shallow**, you can use a **grout** or **filler** to make it look better.\n\n####', '</think>\n\nAbsolutely! The **Allegory of the Cave** is one of the most famous and profound metaphors in Plato\'s *Republic* (Book VII), and it\'s a central part o