DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I learn to do the monkey bars?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'That’s a very good question.  It’s really hard to figure out how to do the monkey bars.  I think the only way is to practice it a lot, but it would be really helpful to have some friends or some good online instructions to follow.  I think you should start by just trying to hold onto the monkey bars and lift yourself up, and then work on making a proper climb.  And then you need to figure out a way to transfer from one side to the other, and maybe find some kind of hanging position to hold yourself in.  But I’m not sure, maybe you could ask some of the friends you have?  Or maybe I could help you figure it out, it would really be helpful.  There’s a lot of really good videos online too, I think you should look for them.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, I will. Any other advice? How can I build strength?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Good question.  I think it’s also really important to build your strength.  I think you should find some way to lift weights, and see if you can make progress, especially when you start to have problems with the monkey bars.  There are some good free online resources, and also maybe you could try doing something that involves throwing balls around, and making an effort to catch them.  And I think the best advice is really to just practice doing these things as much as you can, over and over again.  Just keep trying and practicing, and I’m sure you’ll eventually be able to climb.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, thanks for the motivation.'}]
