DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'I love planets and learning about the solar system in general. Can you tell me the similarities between Earth and Mars?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I can!  Humans have always dreamed of moving off-world to explore.  Mars looks much like the Earth did when it was first forming, but the planet is much colder.  Unfortunately, both planets are quite a bit more violent than they once were.  Mars used to have liquid water on its surface, and was home to many diverse life forms, just like the Earth, but most of the water is now gone.  I believe there are just a few places where Mars could still have flowing water on the surface.  Perhaps humans could try to live there, but they’d have to start all over again and make it look more like their home.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "What's the average temperature of Mars then?"}]
