DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How can I make a piping bag?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Hi! I’m not really sure about this.  What’s a piping bag?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'You put icing in a bag and make flowers with it.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Well that’s very interesting, but it’s not something I’ve heard of before.  Maybe there’s something that I can do to help you out?  What were you thinking?  Maybe a new app can help?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Do you know of an app that knows how to make piping bags?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I don’t, and I’m sorry. I wish there was something more I could do to help.  I wonder, have you looked into it already?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I will try google.  Thanks!'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is it possible to replicate McDonalds french fries at home?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Are you asking about the cooking oil used in McDonald’s French fries? That would be up to you to track down, so it depends on what kind of burger it is. It’s a bit specific. It probably depends on the oil they use for the deep-fryer in the store.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "We're not talking about burgers. But anyway, I do have a deep fryer at home. You think it depends on the kind of oil they use?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The original McDonald’s, the chain that started in Illinois in 1955, used partially hydrogenated vegetable oil. The oil has gone through a process called "partially hydrogenating" to make it more stable. It was used in French fries in addition to other food products.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'And can I find that at a grocery store?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "There are multiple kinds of oils that could be used for deep-frying. It's hard to say without knowing the exact type of oil used by the store. Do you know which one was used for McDonald's French fries? You might try emailing them to find out."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I doubt they would tell me'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I want to make a nice steak dinner, but I don't know the difference between the various cuts of steak."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'OK, I’m happy to help!  I think you want to know which steaks are most tender.  You don’t have to know how to cook the meat itself, just what will be the best.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Yes, exactly!'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Well, there’s a huge range of steaks, but we could start by considering ribeye, which is a very tender cut of meat.  The most tender pieces of meat are in the “loin” of the animal, like the ribeye.  This steak has a thick layer of fat and little connective tissue, which means it will be very tender and juicy.   Also, the ribeye includes the best cut of meat on the cow, called the “short-loin”.  It has lots of marbling, or white lines of fat within the meat, which makes the meat very juicy, and will also have less connective tissue than some other parts of the cow.  Another important consideration is the level of age of the cow, since steak from older cows will be tougher and stringier, since older cows have lost some of their flexibility in their muscles.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, great! What should I serve with steak?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What do I need to start a podcast?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You’ll need a computer, an internet connection, and a microphone.  You might also want to figure out where you want to livestream from, and the URL of your website.  Do you have any existing knowledge or interest in the content you plan to talk about?  What do you hope to achieve by starting a podcast?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Yes. I want to have a podcast that talks about new things people never learned. I want the podcast to be on Apple and have a new one every week. How does livestream work?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You can stream from anywhere you have access to a good internet connection.  You’ll need to make sure that your microphone is working, then you can just record into the microphone and press record, and you’ll be able to record straight into your microphone.  Then you’ll need to upload the audio to your website and promote it on social media.   It’s a long process, but pretty easy once you’re good with it.   Do you have any questions?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay. I was wanting to actually record it so any errors could be edited out. Is that easy to do?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, it is pretty easy to do! It might seem like a time-consuming process, but you’ll get better at it as you go, and it’ll get easier. You just need to make sure to edit all of the audio from the microphones, and not just the part you want people to hear.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is the best microphone to get for a podcast?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I'm thinking about building a garden in my back yard. Can you help with some tips and recommendations?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'What sort of things do you want to grow? Flowers, fruit, or vegetables? Do you have a garden already? Do you want a raised bed garden or just soil? Do you want a fruit or flower tree, or a bush?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I'd like to grow a combination of flowers, herbs, fruit and vegetables. I'd prefer to keep it all the same level."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Sounds like a great choice! I'd recommend a combination of edible flowers, herbs, and vegetables. I recommend sunflowers, nasturtiums, pumpkins, green beans, and some squash. The herbs include basil, thyme, oregano, mint, parsley, and chives."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay. Are they suitable for a temperate European climate?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "It's best to grow plants native to the area you live in, though it is possible to grow plants from warmer or cooler climates. Plants tend to grow bigger in warmer climates and grow smaller or not at all in colder climates. But many plants can be grown in more than one climate. For example, sunflowers are native to North America, while basil is native to Asia. But both are still very popular in many gardens. Some other vegetables which are commonly grown in temperate climates include squash, eggplants, and peppers. I recommend picking plants that are easy to grow, have lots of flowers or fruits, and that taste good."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'That sounds great! Could you also recommend some fruit trees?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "I think you'll find that apples and pears are the most popular fruit trees. Peaches and plums are another choice, and they're usually delicious!"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Great. Do peach and plum trees require certain growing conditions in terms of climate and soil?'}]
