DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you get enough electricity off of solar panels to run your whole house?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Most solar panels generate power with direct sunlight.  So the power they can provide will be reduced when the Sun goes down or during inclement weather.  This means you will likely need to install batteries to store the electricity so that you can use it when the Sun isn’t out.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can I store enough to not need to buy electricity from the utility company?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'This will depend on the amount of energy your solar panels generate during a sunny day, and the charging time of your batteries.  If the amount of power generated is close to the maximum charging rate of your batteries, then you can store it in the batteries to use at night.  If the amount of power generated is close to the maximum amount your batteries can store, then you may be able to store'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'It is pretty sunny where I live.'}]
