DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Should I eat wheat spaghetti instead of flour spaghetti because I have diabetes type 2?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'There are two “causes” of type 2 diabetes.  One is that your body can’t respond properly to insulin, and the other is that the cells of your body have trouble responding to insulin.  The low-carb diet, also known as the ketogenic diet, usually works by encouraging your body to use fat instead of glucose as an energy source.  But it might also be helpful for people with insulin resistance to focus on eating less glucose or starch.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'So, based on your information, should I eat wheat spaghetti instead of flour spaghetti?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Your body will use glucose, or “sugar”, first to fuel your body’s energy needs.  There are other sources of energy for your body, and they’re called “ketones”, but your body can’t switch over to ketones as readily as it can switch over to glucose.  For this reason, wheat spaghetti will give your body a higher amount of glucose, and so will be more likely to keep your blood glucose at the high levels that are risky for you, while flour spaghetti will give you a lower amount of glucose.  That said, it might be worth experimenting with it, and see how your blood glucose responds.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I always thought that wheat spaghetti is healthier than flour spaghetti but you said that it has a higher amount of glucose?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'My pet cat seems to be having a medical emergency. Can you find an emergency veterinarian that is open all night for me?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’m happy to help, but how much do you want to pay?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I'm not really concerned with the price. I just want to get the best medical care as soon as possible!"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The average amount of time between when someone calls for an emergency appointment and when they receive treatment is currently approximately 5 hours.  This means it could take quite a while to get an emergency appointment for a cat.  Do you think this is acceptable?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Do I have a choice? I need to get him the treatment.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I know you are probably concerned about your pet.  I suggest you go to a clinic and see if they can treat him immediately, in case it’s an emergency.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Great. Can you tell me where the nearest emergency clinic is?'}]
