DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Should I invest in the stock market?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Well that’s a hard question.  In general, you want to be informed before you make a big decision like that.  It helps to think carefully about what you are hoping to achieve and how much risk you are willing to take, and what you might lose if the investment goes bad.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay. Any advice?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Well there are lots of different reasons to own stock.  Maybe you’re interested in a company’s future value, or maybe you want to get a percentage of the company’s earnings as a “dividend” payment every year.  Or maybe you want to pay off your mortgage by selling the stock later.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I have a mortgage, but a good amount of money saved. Should I invest in the stock market?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’d say it’s a bad idea to get into the stock market if you’re still saving, or if you have a mortgage and not a lot of other savings.  But if you have your mortgage paid off, or if you have a good amount of savings, then it is a big advantage to be able to earn a dividend, which is a portion of the company’s profits paid out to stockholders every year.  So a good stock to invest in might be one with a high profit margin and a good growth potential.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Which stocks have the best growth potential?'}]
