DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How can I comfort a child whose cat has died?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'My current best guess at what this question is asking for is information about how to respond to a child who is experiencing an event that involves a lot of sadness, and in particular the death of an animal.  Is this correct?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Basically'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'One option to consider would be to talk with the child about how to grieve, since grief is natural and part of the healing process.  Many adults find it helpful to think about or talk about the loss, rather than avoid it.  Maybe you could introduce the idea that there are different ways to deal with difficult things like this, and some people will naturally want to avoid sadness or suppress it, whereas others will find it helpful to deal with their emotions, and also to take a while to process their loss.  The main point is to let the child feel that he or she has some choice about how to handle this situation, since we don’t want to push the child to feel what he or she doesn’t want to feel.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Excellent. What about when the child keeps asking if the pet is gonna come back?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'This is something a parent can probably help with, but you can talk to the child about when animals die, you have to respect their wishes about what you do with their body.  The child may feel attached to the body and wish to keep it in their room for a while.  It’s a good idea to let them think through whether that’s okay or if it would feel strange or make the room feel too sad.  If the child chooses to keep the body around for a while, it’s fine to remind him or her that the body will not come back to life.  You can also help the child remember what the animal’s personality was like, and what it was like to interact with the animal when it was alive.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Well, the pet is now buried.'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I make a safe space for a baby to crawl?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It sounds like the baby is trying to learn how to crawl, and you’re concerned about safety, for example by preventing the baby from crawling into the path of a moving adult or an object in the path.  You might want to try lowering the floor, so that the baby can crawl safely within the area you’ve designated.  Maybe your space could be a safe “cage” where the baby won’t come into harm?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, any other advice?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It might help to think about what this cage looks like and feels like.  You might want to design it with padding and carpeting so the baby can slide and push off the floor.  The floor can be lower, but you also might want to create “safe” barriers so that the baby won’t bump into things or fall into space.  You could also make the cage more colorful, and try to make it a fun space.  I think it’s also helpful to remember that a baby will learn new things, just as you did when you were a baby.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Those are good ideas.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’m happy to help.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Anything else you can tell me?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is a hernia?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'A hernia is an abnormal protrusion or bulging of an organ through a weakened area of tissue. In general, hernias occur when there is an opening between the contents of a hollow, muscle or organ and the outer skin of the body.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Do they tend to be painful?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Some of them do, others don’t.  Sometimes they are just a nuisance.  But when they are severe, they can become large, protrude from the body, and be difficult to ignore.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do they treat them?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'how do i win an ebay auction?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'This is a super broad question, there are lots of different ways you could win. Perhaps your question is specific about how you can bid on an item with your maximum number of bids, or maybe you mean something else?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I want to figure out how to win the item.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Ah, I thought it was something different! How can you win a specific auction on Ebay?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'right'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What are the advantages and disadvantages of rail travel?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "The advantages are that it's safe and enjoyable.  The disadvantages are that it's slow and requires a lot of money."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I don't think it requires a lot of money."}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What are some good sports apparel brands?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'There are many great companies that make sports apparel, but I can recommend some of my favorites.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Sure, please do.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'My first favorite is Nike.  They make a great range of high-quality clothing.  Their brand isn’t just for sporting activities, though, since it also has a strong focus on fashion.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Great, any others you can think of?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The second-best brand is Adidas.  They make fantastic running and training gear.  While I think Nike is better than Adidas for many types of activities, I’ve heard that if you’re into sports, like basketball or soccer, then Adidas is your best bet.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Great, do you have any others you like?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Does wearing a tightly curled permanent wave, in your hair, cause long term hair damage?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’m not sure what you mean by a “tightly curled permanent wave”. Can you explain what you’re referring to?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'When you apply permanent solution to hair, to cause it to permanently wave chemically.'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is a POS system?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Pos (point of sale) is a commonly used term for “point of sale” -- a retail store counter that lets a customer pay for the purchase. The term often is used in retail, where someone is “managing the POS” or just “managing the store” -- by selling things to customers, taking money from them, and keeping track of their purchases. The same applies to things like a restaurant’s counter, where someone is behind it taking customers’ money, and giving change.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'And how does it communicate with a credit or debit card provider?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Good question!  POS systems often communicate with a credit card provider using the small piece of plastic which a customer gives you in exchange for the ability to buy something. This card usually connects to the merchant's phone line, and that phone line will often connect to the internet. At that point, the information on the card is often transmitted through a series of computers, and eventually it gets to the merchant’s bank (or the bank of the merchant’s business partners), where the bank can access the information it has on that customer, like the credit card company. For larger purchases, the bank itself might contact the credit card company."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "So if a store loses its internet connection, the POS system won't work?"}]
