DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I'm trying to get my friend to open up"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sounds great!  What have you tried so far?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I've tried to give my friend a safe space to open up about their feelings but they still aren't comfortable"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It’s really important that people feel safe sharing their feelings, but I totally hear that this isn’t easy for them.  And in my experience, that has a lot to do with them feeling that you can accept them and what they’re saying, even if they’re feeling difficult or uncomfortable feelings.  Do you think you’ve done that, and that they still haven’t opened up?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I have done my best to try to provide a safe space for them, and how they feel but still there is a blocker happening'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'If you’re trying to do your best, maybe what you can try to do is check in with them in a very direct way, and see if you can help them realize that you want to help them.  I know you’ve tried to give them a safe space to open up, but have you also really asked them whether there’s anything you can do to help them open up?  If you take this as your next step, you can think about it like you’re inviting them to tell you something about how they’re feeling, but you’re doing it very directly and without shame or judgment.  It’s like “Hey, I want to help you open up to me, so you can be more open with me.  What can I do to make that easier for you?”  \nIf you try that approach, what do you think will happen?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I feel like that will make them more comfortable and feel more safe to be vulnerable in front of me'}]
