DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'save money for a vacation is there sites to help or advice'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'What I’d recommend is setting up a recurring deposit in your bank account or online banking account. You can find all the information you need online or by going to your bank branch, then the person you talk to can set this up for you. You can then use that money to pay for your vacation or to pay for different expenses, like the first month’s rent on a house or the first months rent of a car. You could also put the money away in your online banking account as a savings account for the future.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Great is there like a site where I could get help withthis'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, there are many websites and online resources that are available to help you with setting up a monthly bank deposit. If you want to know more about the process, just type the question “How do I set up a bank deposit?” into the search box, and several websites with information about how to set up a deposit will come up. I’d recommend one of the first results, which looks like an official government website. That would be a good place to start.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How much should I save'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It depends what you’re saving for, and how much money you make. The first thing you need to know is how much you make per month. Then you can figure out how much to save each month. And you should save a percentage of your monthly income that’s equal to what you’re saving for.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Not sure how to begin'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What kind of tea is popular among the British?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'There are hundreds of types of tea that are popular in the UK!  Some of the more popular teas are English Breakfast Tea, Earl Grey Tea, Ceylon Tea, Assam Tea, Darjeeling Tea, Indian Tea, Irish Breakfast Tea, Oolong Tea, Orange Pekoe Tea, and Japanese Matcha Tea.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Why do they enjoy drinking tea so much'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Most cultures have their own unique teas and their own special brewing traditions and many people in the UK enjoy trying new types of tea and re-discovering old ones.  There are also a lot of English superstitions that tie tea into how people interpret their lives, many of which have to do with keeping calm, coping with a busy life, and social events.  In general it’s safe to say that people in the UK drink tea as a matter of tradition, and because it’s tasty!'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Thank you'}]
