DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is a late fee on a credit card and how do you avoid them?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Late fees are charged by the bank on which you have the credit card, and generally are a percentage of the amount you owe.  The bank doesn’t want to lose money, so they want to ensure that they get paid for the money you owe.  A common practice is to add on a monthly “interest” fee which continues to accrue until you pay the debt off.  As a general rule, it’s better to avoid late fees, since they can quickly eat into your credit score.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "So if you don't pay on time then they charge the late fee?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, usually you pay interest on top of the original balance you owe.  So if you don’t pay at the end of each month, the balance just continues to increase.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "So basically it is better to pay on time so you don't get the late fee and get charged a ton of money."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, it is a good idea to make regular payments on your credit cards, so that you don’t end up with a large balance which the bank might charge a lot of interest for.  It also isn’t wise to go over your credit card limit, since that can cause problems with your credit rating as well.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Which would make you look bad right?'}]
