DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "Hey, my friend is a new mom and has become very quiet in our group chats and not available to hangout. I understand she's building her new family, but I also want to let her know that I'm here to be her friend and support her in this journey"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Well, being a new mom is hard work and can really take a lot of time and energy.  I’m sure your friend will appreciate hearing that you’re always here for her, but you should also really try to accept that sometimes she won’t have time to hang out with you.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Absolutely I do! I do my best to be understanding, I just want to make sure I'm not failing her as a friend"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I think you can also say something like “I’m happy to be there for you as a friend, just know that it’s ok for you to get your space and not always hang out with me.”'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "For sure! I'll shoot her a message this week just to reach out and check in with her and then continue to respect her space"}]
