DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'how does the internet works?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The internet is a network of computers. Users on one computer can communicate with the user on another computer, provided they know the “internet protocol address” of the other computer. This is a numeric address like an email address, but instead of email addresses we use “internet protocol addresses.”'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'what is internet protocol addresses?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Internet protocol addresses are numeric addresses, which computers use to find each other and to send information.  The internet protocol addresses are associated with websites and IP addresses in a specific way, so that when you use your browser to type in a website’s internet protocol address, the browser connects you to that website.  The way internet protocol addresses work depends on the “Internet protocol” that your network uses.  These include IPV4, IPV6, and IPV6+2.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I don't unders can you explain the internet in"}]
