DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I'm going to lend someone some money, but want to draw up a contract first. How do I make a legally binding one?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Gosh, that’s a tough question.  What I hear you saying is that you want to make sure your friend and you can’t mess up the deal.  I think that you’re already thinking that you have to draw up a contract.  Do you want to talk about what would go in the contract?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Yes, I just want to make sure the person I lend the money to pays me back, so I want a contract between the two of us.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Oh!  I thought you meant, you wanted a contract with a third party, like the government or the bank, to make sure they could enforce payment, but you just want to write the contract with the person you’re lending the money to.  OK, so that would be really similar to the agreement you make with a bank or the government, but between just the two of you, not involving a third party.  So what would go in a contract like that?  What would you want to know?  I can help you write it down.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Well, I just want to know how to make a contract legally binding.'}]
