DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do you keep a good credit score?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'What you do in terms of keeping your credit score, is to make payments on the loans you have, and then avoid taking out new loans.   And of course keep track of all the information for your credit report.  Then if your credit score falls to a certain point, you can get it re-evaluated and try to get it improved.  If you have lots of loans, that can be hard, and the only way to really improve your score is to pay off more loans and then get new loans for other things.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "So keep paying your loans. Don't get new ones if you can?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, exactly.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is there anything else you can do?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'There are some other things you can do, like consider a new credit card, but those usually don’t work that well.   You may be able to save up and then get a card with an introductory interest rate.   If you do get a new card, pay the bill before the due date.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Ok thank you very much.'}]
