DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Which foods have a long shelf life?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I would recommend stockpiling non-perishable foodstuffs like:'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How long will these products last when stored?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Stocking a small amount of these products will provide you with a basic store of non-perishable foods for a year or more, if properly stored.  A larger store of these foods will provide enough nourishment for around a year and a half.  The time period will depend on the size of the store and the quality of its preservation.  I can offer more detail on each product’s exact shelf life, but will you be needing that?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Yes, I would like that information if you have it.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Brown rice has a shelf life of about five years in the refrigerator.  It can also be stored for longer periods of time in cold temperatures.  Pasta has a shelf life of about a year, though after a year it should be replaced.  Oatmeal can last up to ten years in a dry, cool place, though one year is more common.  Whole grain bread has a shelf life of around two years.  Granola bars have a shelf life of around two years, if stored correctly.  Jams and jellies can last about two years, also if stored correctly.  Dried meat can last for about a year if stored correctly, though it has a shorter shelf life if it’s not kept dry.  Canned and frozen meats can last around two years, depending on the type.  Powdered milk has a shelf life of around two years.  Canned and frozen fruits and vegetables can last around three years, though a few months of refrigeration will help them to last longer.  Beef jerky has a shelf life of around two years, and even longer if properly stored.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'This information helped me a lot. I will make notes of all of this.'}]
