DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I use a fitness step tracker to monitor my daily activity?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I have two suggestions: You could check out an app for your phone, such as the one I’ve heard of called “Fitbit”; or you could buy a stand-alone step tracker that connects to your computer or smartphone.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay can you tell me how to use the app for a phone version.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sure, if you have an app on your phone that connects with your computer, it would be best to get it from the app store rather than the website.  The app would need to be installed on your computer, and that could be done through a USB cord from your computer to your phone, or by “wirelessly” (as they call it) through the app’s native software that communicates with the computer.   You would then go to the app store’s website (it should be easy to find) and find the app for the tracker you want to buy.   You would then install that.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'No I just want one that works with my smart phone only.'}]
