DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How can I explain the concept of science to a child'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'If you want to explain the concept of science to a child, you could start by defining it for yourself.  In the age of big data and exponential increases in computing power, we’re better at designing hypotheses and testing them than ever before, and our ability to combine our ideas about the world has increased exponentially.  It’s exciting, but that doesn’t mean there’s a need to “sell” it to a child.  Tell them instead about how we learn things, and how it’s possible to figure things out about the world by reasoning about it and making observations and comparisons.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Any other ideas?'}]
