DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I'm planning to learn how to cook Chinese food.  Any suggestions?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Wow, that's very ambitious!  Do you have any existing knowledge of Asian cuisine?"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Well, I eat regularly at Asian restaurants.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "It's a pretty big leap from regular dining out to being able to cook at home yourself.  What is your learning style? Do you prefer formal or informal instruction, or can you learn best from watching others?"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I want to start with simple recipes.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "The first thing you'll want to do is take a class or watch YouTube videos about basic Chinese cooking technique.  Once you know how to chop things and steam things and make dumplings, it's easy to create your own recipes.  \nHave you thought about what you might like to cook?  \nA lot of people start with trying to make a bowl of rice, but you can really get creative and invent your own recipes.  \nHere's a recipe I found online:"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Noodles in fried rice?  I have never heard that.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Chinese restaurants often make fried rice with leftover cold noodles, and that\'s the best way to go.  I think with noodles and eggs and things it\'s fun to just "throw it all in the pot" together.  \nThen you\'ll want to cook until the noodles are soft and "al dente".  I would probably use around a half a cup of oil for the whole pan of fried rice, and maybe add another half-cup or so.  Also, if you can find a vegetarian stir-fry sauce, it would be great for making fried rice.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I don't think so.  They make fried rice with leftover ice and not noodle."}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is Tracfone a good prepaid plan?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I think it is pretty good if you don’t travel. It’s definitely not good if you’re planning to travel outside of the US or even into Canada because there are special SIM cards you need to buy. It’s also important that you get an international plan because it is very easy to end up with an international charge if you’re not paying attention.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Ok that is good to think about. International travel could be more I would not want that.'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do you switch to a different user account in Win 10?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Which version of Windows 10 are you using?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '64 bit Home Edition'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You’ll find this information in the “Login and Sign-in” settings.   Here’s a direct link:  https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/uwp/custom-ui/settings/user-accounts?view=windows-10-uwp#common-settings-account'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Link didn't work. Just describe the process please."}]
