DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How can I protect my hearing?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Great question! There are many ways to help with hearing loss. One possibility is to get regular hearing tests from an audiologist. And some hearing loss can be treated with hearing aids.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How loud should I listen to my music in headphones?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You should probably limit yourself to listening to music at around 80 decibels. At higher volumes it’s more likely you’ll have hearing damage.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I find out which level of volume oh my phone is 80 decibels?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You could find the decibel level at each volume level on your phone, and then average them all together to find the average. But there are some other ways, too. A good online decibel calculator might also work for you.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Thanks for the help!'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is the easiest musical instrument to learn how to play?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The easiest instrument to learn is the piano.  If you are curious about learning to play it yourself, you might want to try some of my recommended lessons on this page: \nhttps://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=pianointended.piano&hl=en'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'The link leads me nowhere. What is the easiest instrument to play or the easiest for beginners?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The best recommendation I have for you is to try the piano.  Other recommendations might include guitar, ukulele, or violin.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Aren't pianos expensive though?"}]
