Initial completions: ["</think>\n\nTo empty the spam folder in Microsoft Outlook, follow these steps:\n\n---\n\n### **1. Open Outlook**\n- Launch Microsoft Outlook (either the desktop version or the web version).\n\n---\n\n### **2. Access the Spam Folder**\n- Click on the **Folder** tab (or **View** in the ribbon).\n- Right-click on the **Spam** folder, then select **Move to** or **Move to a Different Folder**.\n- Alternatively, you can directly open the **Spam** folder by typing its name (usually the folder is called **Spam**) in the **Folder** pane.\n\n---\n\n### **3. Empty the Spam Folder**\n- Once you've opened the **Spam** folder, you can:\n  - **Right-click** the spam folder and select **Delete** (this removes the folder and all its contents from the mail system).\n  - Or, if you want to just **empty** the contents (not delete the folder), you can:\n", "</think>\n\nThat's a really thought-provoking question. Let's break it down carefully.\n\n### 1. **Why is the idea of not finding a new energy source so concerning?**\n\nFor the next 100 years, **electricity is the core of human civilization**. Everything—from lighting homes to powering cars and computers—relies on electricity. If we can't find a new energy source, we'll be stuck with the same problems:\n\n- **Energy scarcity**: We'll be constrained by the amount of energy we can generate and distribute.\n- **Costs**: Electricity is expensive to produce and transport. Higher costs could lead to:\n  - **Higher energy prices** (which would affect industries, businesses, and even everyday life).\n  - **Limited expansion** of infrastructure, such as roads, railways, or data centers.\n- **Environmental impact**: We might continue using fossil fuels, which are unsustainable and harmful to the planet.\n- **Global inequality**: If energy", '</think>\n\nAbsolutely! The Lower East Side of New York City is a vibrant and eclectic neighborhood with a rich cultural scene, a variety of food options, and a lot of spots that to