DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is deep cleaning teeth?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I recommend our interactive FAQ for more information.  Here is a diagram of the human teeth:'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "My dentist said that my teeth need deep cleaning.  I'm not sure what it is."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Deep cleaning is one of the major ways that dentists can make sure your teeth are healthy and that you can get rid of gunk between the teeth and at the gum line.  Many types of bacteria live in your mouth, including mouth bacteria, and in order to keep them under control, dentists need to deep clean teeth every few months.  By doing this, they can get rid of plaque which may be causing tooth decay or gum disease.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'It is so expensive compared to regular cleaning.  Why is that?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Deep cleaning is the most thorough method of cleaning and can be quite expensive.  In some countries, like in the US, there is an argument in the dental community about whether deep cleaning should be standard practice.  However, some countries like Switzerland, have found that by using deep cleaning regularly, the cost of treatment in the long term is actually significantly less than regular cleaning, which is also much more effective.  There is also a cost to human life, as patients with gum disease, and periodontal disease have a much higher risk of heart disease and diabetes.  In these cases, deep cleaning becomes a life-saving procedure.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'After listening to you, I guess I need to make an appointment with my dentist.'}]
