DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you tell me what the difference is between an anxiety attack and just feeling stressed out?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Oh, that’s a great question! Anxiety and stress can often feel very similar, but in fact they’re quite different experiences. Stress is usually a response to a particular thing that’s happening in your life - maybe something is happening in your life that you don’t really feel like you can handle. Anxiety, on the other hand, is a state of body and mind where you feel very uncertain about everything, and this includes future events as well as things that are happening in the present moment. When you have an anxiety attack, you tend to feel anxious about many things at once, and often it’s hard to even notice the specific causes of your anxiety.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I see. Does anxiety also cause more physical reactions that being stressed does?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, there’s a lot of overlap between the anxiety symptoms and those of the stress reaction, so I often recommend paying close attention to your physical symptoms if you suspect you might be having an anxiety attack. Does your heart feel like it’s beating very fast, or racing even? Do you feel queasy or dizzy? Do you feel like you might be hyperventilating? These physical symptoms can be a warning sign of an anxiety attack, so it’s good to know what they look like.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'And what about panic attacks? Are they the same as an anxiety attack?'}]
