DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What should I pack to go to a water park?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I think you’re asking me for a recommendation of what things to bring to a water park, and what things you might want to pack.  So I think the best recommendation I can give you is that it’s fun to go in the water, and be careful with slippery surfaces in the water.  I also want to remind you that if you get in water at a water park, or any other place, you should wear water shoes and not go barefoot.  The slide at the water park will be a slippery surface, and I recommend water shoes.  I don’t recommend wearing flip flops in the water park, because the water will get inside your shoes and they won’t provide you with adequate protection, and you could potentially get an infection.  You should also watch for sharp objects, since they may be a hazard at the water park.  You should have a towel with you, because you may get very wet and need to dry off.  You should also have sunscreen with you, and I recommend a hat, as well as lots of water.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What should I bring to prevent covid?'}]
