DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Tell me about smallpox.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It was a terrible disease, very dangerous to get. It could kill you, or leave you scarred for life. It’s spread by droplets when someone coughs or sneezes, so you can get it from being near someone who is sick. It’s hard to get rid of smallpox, and vaccination became very important. It’s hard to trace the origins of vaccination, but the basic idea has been around since Ancient Egypt. It was developed by Edward Jenner in the late 18th century, after he took note of the fact that people who contracted cowpox rarely contracted smallpox.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What was the death rate for smallpox?'}]
