DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How long was World War One?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The First World War lasted from July 28, 1914 to November 11, 1918. In September 1914, the German Army invaded Belgium and a month later France declared war on Germany, and as a result, the British Army entered the war as well. In the Spring of 1915, the Germans launched a large-scale offensive in France, and that summer, the British joined the French in a counterattack on the Western Front. By the end of 1916, the main fronts in France and Belgium had stabilized, and they remained relatively unchanged for the next two years. Meanwhile, in the Eastern Front, the Russians, facing pressure from the Central Powers (Germany and Austria-Hungary), had reached the Treaty of Brest-Litovsk with the Central Powers, ending Russia’s involvement in the war.  This put the Central Powers in a better position on the Western Front, and in the Spring of 1918, they launched a new offensive. They advanced across a wide front, forcing the'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Who all fought in World War One?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The belligerents were as follows:'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'When did the Americans enter World War One?'}]
