DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How can I teach someone to avoid falling for phishing scams?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Tell them not to use an account with username “username” or password “password”.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What else can people look for to avoid email scams?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'As a rule of thumb, beware of any email that purports to be from “Amazon” and contains the words “Web Form”, “Credit Card” or “Sweepstakes”.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is there any way to block those types of emails?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I just adopted a new kitten but I'm worried about introducing her to my existing cat.  Do you have any advice?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "The best way to understand a new cat's personality is to observe how they interact with your existing cat, and with other cats you might encounter.  A new kitten can try out all the same behaviors with your existing cat, such as climbing on top of them, pawing at their face, and kneading with their paws."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Would it be helpful to bring something with the kitten's scent on it for my existing cat to smell first?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "That's a great idea!  When the cat gets used to the new cat's smell, they might be more willing to interact with them.  It's also a good idea to minimize interaction for a few days while they get used to each other, since cats can often misread or misinterpret feline social cues."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What should I do if my existing cat gets aggressive with the kitten?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "It can be hard to tell what's going on when you're watching a confrontation between cats that don't yet know each other.  If they're doing something like baring their teeth, hissing, pawing at the air, or swatting at each other, that's usually a sign they're scared or are angry.  But it might also mean they're simply excited to meet.  It might also just be a misunderstanding, since some cats have more dominant personalities.  It can be helpful to take pictures of the cats interacting and to consult with a vet or cat behavior expert about how to interpret what's happening.  I'm not a cat expert, but I'm happy to try to help you understand what's happening when I see a video of it."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Should I give them separate food to start?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What are some hearty recipes for mac and cheese?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'All the recipes on the internet are very variable in terms of quantities, ingredients, or even types of cheese, but they are mostly along the lines of this:'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Sounds delicious. Do you recommend whole grain or regular macaroni?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'If you have a high carbohydrate tolerance, the whole grain version is best.  You might want to try adding peas and green onions to the recipe for some additional nutrients.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'That sounds interesting.'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'I have to make something for a church baked sale. What are some popular baked goods that are easy to sell at a bake sale?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Wow, it sounds like you’re really excited to have the opportunity to sell baked goods at a bake sale! I would guess that cinnamon rolls are very popular, though there are also lots of options if you’re worried that they may not sell well. I’ve heard that a lot of churches also like cupcakes, and there are many options you could choose from there.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Those sound good! What are some of the most popular types of cupcakes?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What are some interesting things in nature I could sketch?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I know a place where there is a great concentration of songbirds who regularly perform aerial displays.  If you like, I can guide you there and take photos and videos that you can use for your sketching, as long as you’ll allow me to watch from a safe distance.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'That sounds good. What other things could I draw?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What kind of foods should I feed my pet turtle?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Turtles are omnivores, and there’s really no limit to what you can feed them.  Some examples of good foods are lettuce, carrots, sweet potatoes, strawberries, or cucumbers.  It’s okay if they grow soft and mushy, and to some extent this might even be good for the turtles since it makes food easier to eat.  On the other hand, don’t give your turtle cooked foods like bacon or raw eggs.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'It seems like they have a wide range of foods that they can eat.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, they can eat pretty much any kind of plant or animal.  If you put fresh spinach in their water, or corn on the cob, they’ll eat that too.  Turtles have a wide variety of digestive enzymes that can work with a wide range of foods, even including those they aren’t very used to eating.  If you were to eat a bowl of asparagus for example, turtles would have no problem eating a bowl of fresh spinach afterwards.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'It is probably a good idea to give them a lot of leafy greens, right?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, your turtles will be healthier if they have a wide variety of plant foods.  But if you feed them only leafy greens, they might get bored and eat less food overall.  So there’s a middle ground: it’s usually good to have some variety in what you feed them, but it’s also good to have some variety in the food itself.  So if you don’t like kale, for example, you can substitute spinach, which is also a great leafy green.  And some people have really good luck feeding their turtles a range of different colored foods, like lettuce, broccoli, corn, squash, and carrots.  So, leafy greens are good and variety is good, but don’t be afraid to try new foods if you find a good one.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'You said they are omnivores. What kind of animals do they eat? I guess things like worms and bugs?'}]
