mend checking with the business directly or looking at their website for the most up-to-date details. They may have valet parking or a designated parking area, but I can't confirm that right now.", "</think>\n\nCertainly! Lucid dreaming is a fascinating phenomenon where the dreamer becomes aware that they are dreaming and can then control the dream's content, storyline, and even their environment. It's a state that many people explore as a form of self-reflection, creativity, and even therapy.\n\nHere's a brief overview of lucid dreaming:\n\n---\n\n### **What is Lucid Dreaming?**\n\n- **Definition**: A dream in which the dreamer is consciously aware that they are dreaming.\n- **How It Works**: It involves recognizing one's own actions and thoughts during the dream, and then using that awareness to influence the dream's direction.\n- **Types**: There are different types of lucid dreaming, such as:\n  - **Realized lucid dreaming** (where you are consciously aware you're dreaming)\n  - **Unrealized lucid dreaming** (where you are aware you're dreaming but don't control the dream)\n\n---\n\n### **How to Practice Lucid Dreaming", '<think>\n\n</think>\n\nDolphins are indeed very smart, and they are often regarded as one of the most intelligent animals in the ocean. Here are some key points that highlight their intelligence:\n\n1. **Complex Communication**: Dolphins use a variety of vocalizations and body language to communicate with one another. They can recognize and respond to the sounds of other dolphins, and some species even use tools in their environment, like using objects to extract food.\n\n2. **Tool Use**: While not as well-documented as in some other animals, dolphins have been observed using tools in certain contexts. For example, they might use objects to pry open shells or to retrieve food.\n\n3. **Problem-Solving**: Dolphins have been shown to solve puzzles and use tools in experiments. They can also remember the locations of food sources for extended perio