DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you give me some recommendations for a first date?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sure, let’s get the practical details out of the way: you might want to dress up a bit, but casual is good too. Go somewhere nice, but not too fancy; you don’t want to be judged for trying too hard, or too little. You should probably find a place that’s local to you, since public transit is the most practical way to get around. Maybe order in some food or drinks, but it’s definitely fine to go out for dinner too! Have a nice conversation, ask questions, find out about your interests and concerns and more about each other’s lives. Try to think of a positive action, such as bringing some flowers or chocolate or a thoughtful note, that will show you are a considerate, thoughtful person.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay. Going out for dinner sounds like a good option. We barely know each other, so would it be best to go somewhere more affordable?'}]
