er the U.S. government lied about Iraq possessing Weapons of Mass Destruction (WMDs) is a complex and contentious issue with historical and political significance. Here's a structured analysis:\n\n### 1. **Background of the WMD Claims**\n   - The U.S. government, under the **Bush Administration**, claimed that Iraq possessed **nuclear, chemical, and biological WMDs**. These claims were central to the **2003 invasion of Iraq**, justified by the need to eliminate weapons of mass destruction and prevent threats to U.S. security.\n   - The **September 2002 report** by the **Iraqi WMDs Task Force** (led by the U.S. Department of State and the Pentagon) concluded that Iraq **did not possess WMDs**. The administration later issued a **false claim** (in the 2003 invasion) that Iraq had **nuclear weapons**, which was later debunked"]
