DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'how do i know if my child is ready for a sibling?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'What does it mean to be “ready”?  I think that’s a really complex question that you should approach in a lot of different ways, rather than looking for a single answer.  Do you want to feel confident in your ability to care for your child, regardless of whether or not they have a sibling?  Do you want to know that you have everything you need to be prepared for a new child?  Do you want to make sure you’re not rushing into having another child too soon?  Or do you want to have a sibling, and you'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "i want them to get along and i don't want my firstborn to be traumatized or neglected"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Okay, so it sounds like your priority is to minimize trauma for your firstborn, and your second priority is that your second child gets the love and attention that you have to give.  Do you want to know whether it’s worth going through the experience of becoming a family of three right now, or should you wait?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'yeah i want to know signs that my child is ready'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you recommend me a band that sounds similar to In Flames?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Well I think that In Flames is often referred to as the “Swedish Metallica”, so maybe if you want something with that vibe, you might want to look into Rammstein.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you tell me a little bit more about Rammstein?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Rammstein was formed in 1993 in Berlin by songwriter and lead singer Till Lindemann, vocalist Richard Kruspe, guitarist Paul Landers, and bassist Oliver Riedel.  They began their career playing the heavy metal genre but have since crossed over into many other genres.  They started out as being a kind of “Iron Maiden-esque” band, but have now gone on to create everything from electronic to techno and pop.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is their most popular album?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'My husband works very hard at his job and is often stressed and tired. How can I show him I appreciate how hard he works?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’m really glad you asked. This is actually a complex question and my personal opinion is that I would get as involved with his work as possible.  This could mean doing things like cooking and cleaning for him, and/or being his sounding board when he comes home from work so he can discuss his problems.  But I’m not sure this is a problem you want to solve, as doing more things for him will probably just increase his workload.  I’m just not sure it’s the best approach to the problem you’re having.  Is that enough information?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What approach would you suggest?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’m not sure I can think of any.  My recommendation would be to figure out what he wants from his job and see if that would help you to better support him.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, that sounds good. What kind of comfort meal would you suggest I make for him?'}]
