DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "The ice in my freezer has an off taste and I don't like to use it. Do you know of any tips that can help keep ice fresh?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I would recommend having a bigger freezer.  People generally get fewer than 10 pounds of ice per visit, and most places make ice, to their standard of quality, to serve you 20 pounds. So if you have a small freezer, you will have to make more trips to your store or bar, and be more careful about getting the right amount of ice.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'No, no. I mean, the ice cubes in my ice tray taste nasty'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Ice cubes are a bit of a funny one, and really depend on the particular ice cubes. If they have been in your freezer for a long time, they might have a bit of extra moisture which is making them less fresh.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Eh, I feel like they taste nasty right away. The first day or two after completely freezing'}]
