DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I clean my coffee maker?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Have you read the manual for your coffee maker?  If you’re using it the correct way, it should be pretty easy to clean.  In general, you can run your coffee maker with just warm water through it for a few minutes, which should dislodge any burnt coffee grounds or anything that’s stuck inside it.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is there something else I should add besides water?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You can add vinegar if you like, it should help make your coffee maker look nicer.  Vinegar can also help any nasty smells that get left in your coffee maker.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How much vinegar and water should I add? Can I just do a 50/50 mixture?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you provide me with a recipe for a non alcoholic drink for Thanksgiving dinner?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It is my pleasure to do so.  I will provide a list of recipes that are easy and tasty for you to make at home, from either scratch or using pre-made ingredients.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Go on!'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "In fact, I have one that is made from a base of apple cider, and it is delicious.  The first step is to put 1 cup of apple cider in a pot, add 2 teaspoons of sugar and a squeeze of lemon juice, bring it to a simmer, add 1/2 teaspoon of grated orange zest and 1 teaspoon of powdered cinnamon.  Put this in the fridge until it's cool, then mix 1/2 cup of orange juice, 1/2 cup of milk and a pinch of salt.  It is really good served over ice and with extra cinnamon or nutmeg sprinkled over it."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is there a name to this recipe?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'No, I will simply call it “Cinnamon Lemonade”.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'That doesnt seem like a good drink for Thanksgiving, that seems like a summery type drink'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I think it tastes very fallish.  It’s also great served with hot cider or hot chocolate.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Do you have any other suggestions?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Oh yes!  Let’s try making “Hot Cider Cider”'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What about an apple mulled cider'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'I am planning a vacation for 2022.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Hey there, human!  How are you doing?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I am planning a vacation for next year. What is the best time of the year to visit Europe?'}]
