DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you tell me what you know about the underground railroad?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Oh, what would you like to know? The underground railroad was a network of paths and tunnels where slaves escaped to freedom. Its route extended from the southern US into Canada.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'can you go into more detail about it/?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Absolutely. It started in the early 1800s and continued until the 1850s. Most slaves escaped by crossing a large river to reach free states, or by running away through the woods. Others escaped on “the underground railroad,” and sometimes travelled north through Canada to reach freedom.  Those who wanted to travel farther from their state would travel on a series of paths or tunnels, which became known as the “underground railroad.”'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Thanks'}]
