DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Are Red Foxes native to North America?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, and so are raccoons, red squirrels, porcupines, and opossums.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Have people learned how to domesticate Red Foxes?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'They have, in fact, been domesticated by many native American cultures, and you can see them at festivals and stores all over the United States.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What kind of food do domesticated Red Foxes eat?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'They have adapted well to many types of foods, and so the human owners need only provide food that is good for their fur and health.  Common types of food include all kinds of fruits and vegetables, meats, fish, and of course dog food.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is it illegal to own a Red Fox in America?'}]
