DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How does rinse aid in a dishwasher work?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Great question!  In this type of dishwasher, as the water in the machine cycles through the heating stage, it heats up and then gets pushed out through the washer nozzles and into the dishwasher tub.  Rinse aid powder is added into the washer at this stage and reacts with the water in the washer to create a thick foam that’s sprayed onto the dishes.  This foam removes residual food from the dishes.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What happens to the residual foam?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The foam remains inside the dishwasher.  After about 30 minutes it becomes clear and disappears.  It’s safe to do this because it does not contain soap.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'But my dishwasher is in my kitchen not a hotel'}]
