DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do people make money on Youtube?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Youtube pays the video creators some money, but also all kinds of people take money from advertising displayed on the videos.  In a “classic” Youtube scenario, when a viewer watches a video the creator gets paid a small percentage of whatever the advertising is worth, and sometimes the creator gets a fixed fee for uploading a video.  The creator also gets a small amount of money for every person who clicks “like” on a video, and every person who shares a video with a friend or subscribers.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'So there are several ways then. That is quite interesting.'}]
