DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How can I learn to juggle?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Juggling is a difficult skill, because a good juggle requires you to be able to keep three or more balls in the air.  I can tell you that it will help to practice, and to look at how professional jugglers do it.  Are you aware that people who juggle professionally are called “juggling masters”?  One technique that helps is if you focus on your breathing when you’re juggling, because when you’re focused on keeping the balls in the air, it can sometimes be difficult to breath.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Should I start with two balls and then add a third?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I think it would be helpful if you practiced each of the techniques one at a time, instead of mixing them.  If you focus on one ball at a time, it can be easier to learn.  Here’s one way to practice:  Start by juggling one ball, and try to get the ball in the air and keep it in the air as many times as possible.  At first it might be easier to keep the ball in the air if you keep your hands apart.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'That sounds really helpful.  How long will it take before I can juggle three balls?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It depends on how much you practice.  It might take a month or more to get the technique, but you could start with two balls and practice one ball at a time and keep practicing for a week or two.  I’ve seen people juggling 3 balls after just one month of practice.   It’s hard to predict exactly how long it will take you, but you might start with one ball and then move up to two, and then add a third.  What do you think?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Thanks, I will try to practice really hard!'}]
