DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you give me a rundown of what caused the Great Depression?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The Great Depression began with the stock market crash of 1929. People who had invested in the stock market were disappointed that the value of their shares had fallen, and they lost faith in the economy. The economy started to contract. Businesses weren’t making as much money, and so they laid off workers and reduced the wages of those who remained. Households saw their income shrink, which made it harder to pay their mortgages, which in turn created a downward spiral in the housing market. This decreased aggregate demand for goods and services, and eventually led to the “Great Depression”.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Was the great depression a global depression like the economic crash of 2008 was? Or was American the main one affected.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The Great Depression had a global impact. In fact, in many countries the effects of the Great Depression were even more severe than in the United States.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I didn't know that. Which countries suffered the most?"}]
