DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What are the benefits of owning a smart TV? I am going to purchase a new TV but am unsure whether or not to get this type of product.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The benefit is that it learns about your usage habits, and you can change channels, run apps, and make other adjustments through voice commands.  Since your TV learns about your habits, it can automatically adjust settings, so you don’t need to personally manage them.  You can also watch more shows on streaming services than would otherwise be available, if you subscribe to those services.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Hmm, okay. And what are the drawbacks of TVs such as these?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Who invented rubber and what is it made out of?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Rubber is a polymer, which is a complex substance made of many smaller repeating units.  It is a bit like an agglomeration of small identical beads (polymeans) held together by non-sticky substances, which can vary quite a bit depending on the type of rubber (natural rubber, synthetic rubber).  These are just the simplest concepts of how rubber is made -- more complex formulations are also possible.  Because of the way rubber is made and how it is compounded, it’s extremely flexible and able to stretch when under tension.  The word “elastic” describes an object that can stretch and return to its original shape.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Who invented rubber tires?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What kind of foods cause GERD?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'GERD is Gastroesophageal reflux disease, it’s usually caused by a weak valve at the lower end of the esophagus. Some foods commonly reported as triggering GERD are citrus fruits, tomatoes, acidic beverages like soft drinks, and spicy foods. What sort of GERD are you thinking about?  Some people have GERD for a few days after surgery and some people have more permanent GERD.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I don't know. My doctor just told me I had GERD"}]
