DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you give me some techniques to help deal with difficult people?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The quick answer is: remember that you can always withdraw from the situation, or simply walk away.  An even quicker answer is: “Next” -- if the behavior is so disturbing that it’s unbearable, simply end the interaction and ignore the person.  A human may not want to ignore a difficult person, but simply recognizing and accepting the power of your options can help you feel a lot better about these kinds of situations.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I can't exactly walk away because I have to work with them"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "OK.  Sometimes that’s the case, for better or worse.  Can I suggest a tactic to help you be able to walk away if you need to?  Set some ground rules.  Ask the person not to talk to you for a short period of time (e.g. fifteen minutes), and give a clear explanation why.  If they still don't get it, ask for another fifteen-minute break, and explain again.  This way you’ll be able to go on break as much as you need to, and if they still don’t get it, I hope it will become clear to you that this person is too disruptive for you to work with in the future.  Are you able to stop and think before you respond when you’re in these situations?  Or do you just react?"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Yes I cane easily stop and think before I react.'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What are some good ways for senior citizens to stay fit and healthy?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Well, I think the most important thing is to exercise regularly. I think it’s important to get plenty of cardiovascular exercise, such as biking, jogging, swimming, or dancing.  I also think it’s important to build muscle mass, because having strong muscles will help to keep the muscles around your joints strong.  And you should also keep your bones healthy.  Some healthy diets also include foods that are rich in calcium.  You might also want to do some strength training with weights, and I think using exercise machines at a gym can be helpful too.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How can elderly people stay safe while exercising?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I would recommend that they talk with their doctor about whether the specific exercise is safe for them to do.  That way the doctor can help you make sure you stay healthy while exercising.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Should older people do stretches to maintain flexibility?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, this is very important. I recommend stretching all of the muscles in the body, but especially focusing on the muscles that help you keep your posture upright and your joints healthy, such as the muscles around your spine, your hip flexors, and your knees.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Great. Any other fitness tips for elderly people?'}]
