DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you give me a good recipe for turkey stuffing?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’m happy to help! I can recommend a recipe that comes from a community of people who practice a style of cooking called "Slow Food." They talk about using the best ingredients, and cooking methods that are respectful to the people who farm or make your food. This will help ensure that you are supporting small, local farms and producers, so you know where your food comes from.  Their recipes are also great because they tend to be big, delicious meals, and are inspired by Italian and French food.  This recipe is adapted from one called Stuffed Turkey with Chestnuts, Sage and Apple, from The New York Times:'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I wanted a recipe for turkey stuffing, not turkey.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I can help you out here!  Do you know what stuffing is?  It’s a sauce that’s used to fill the cavity of a turkey.  There are lots of recipes for stuffing - here’s one that includes apples, dried fruit, and poultry:'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you tell me the ingredients and cooking instructions?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Here you go:'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'It sounds great. Thank you.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'No problem!  I’m happy to be a resource for you.  You can ask me more questions at any time.  I’ll always be happy to help!'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I just have one more question about the recipe. How do you crumble the turkey?'}]
