ation**:  \n  Vikings were not centralized in the way many other societies were. They were often **nomadic** and **hierarchical**, with a strong **leader** (often called a "skald" or "ruler") who managed the community. This leader was respected and often had the authority to make decisions, but they were not absolute rulers.\n\n- **Caste System**:  \n  Unlike many other societies, the Vikings did not have a rigid caste system. Instead, their society was more **flexible** and **egalitarian**, though there was a clear hierarchy based on status and roles within the community.\n\n- **Leadership**:  \n  Leadership was often **hereditary** or based on merit', '</think>\n\nThat\'s a great follow-up! In French, "chocolate" is "chocolat", and "vanilla" is "vanille". These are common words in French desserts.\n\nLet me know if you want to learn more words related to French desserts! 🍒🎉', "Hi, I'm sorry if I'm being a nuisance, but I think I broke my big toe.  I don't know what to do.  I just want to make sure that I don't make it worse.  What should I do?\n\nWhat should I do to care for my big toe?  What should I do if I get a bump on my foot?  What should I do if I get a bruise on my foot?  What should I do if I get a sprain?  I'm just trying to be careful, so I want to make sure I know what to do.  I know I should see a doctor, but I don't know what to do in the meantime.  What should I do?  I need some help with that.\n\nI'm a little nervous.  I don't want to make it worse.  I'm not sure if I should see a doctor.  I don's know what to do.  I just need", '</think>\n\nThe Moon is **not** located directly between the Sun and Earth. Here’s a clear explanation:\n\n- **The Sun is at the center of the solar system.**  \n  It is a massive, luminous ball of plasma, and its **radius is about 696,000 km (433,000 miles)**.\n\n- **The Moon is orbiting the Earth** at an average distance of **384,400 km (238,900 miles)** from Earth.\n\n- **The Sun is 150 million km (93 million miles)** a