DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I clean a coffee maker?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The two options for cleaning a coffee maker are a wash cycle, and a soak cycle. For each, the coffee maker comes out of the machine. For the wash cycle, you start by spraying the inside of the coffee maker with some liquid dish soap and water, then run a cycle of hot water through the machine until all the dishes and utensils are clean.  Then you need to dry the inside of the machine, and clean the counter tops.  For the soak cycle, you start by spraying the inside of the coffee maker with some liquid dish soap and water, then run a cycle of hot water through the machine until all the dishes and utensils are clean.  Then you need to remove all the dishes and utensils from the machine, and allow the water to soak for ten to thirty minutes.  Then you need to wipe the inside of the machine, and dry the inside.  After that you can clean the counter tops.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can I use vinegar to run through the machine?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, you can.  Simply turn on the machine, and run some vinegar through.  If the vinegar helps with the buildup of gunk on the machine, then you can use it frequently to help maintain your machine.  If vinegar doesn’t help clean your machine, you may have to use an actual cleaning product or product from your coffee machine’s manufacturer.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Thanks a lot for the answers I needed.'}]
