DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "Hi, I'd like to sell my old vinyl records on eBay. How do I do that?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Well you need to make a category for them in eBay, and a description for each one.  You can also upload pictures of the items, and write a description for each picture.  It might be nice to have some information about how old the records are, and perhaps you can rate them with a score.  You can also, for example, enter other information like price, condition, size, and whether they're in perfect condition or not.  See here for more information about what eBay considers “Seller’s Marks” -- that’s what you can say in your description of what each record is, and it's all entirely optional: http://help.ebay.com/customer/mail-thankyou/helpitem.html/29083/Condition-and-Collectibility"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Thanks. Any tips for how to handle shipping. or how to get good prices for what I sell?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "What's the best way to teach English to someone who doesn't know the language?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "I'm not a teacher, but I am a language learner, so I might be able to help with that.   I'm not familiar with English, though, so my initial recommendation is that you describe your exact goal and your goals with your target language.  I also suggest you clarify the learning environment, whether you want to work on English outside of the context of school, or in school, or at home.  What are your priorities, and which language learning methods will you use?  What resources will you use?   Are you focusing on vocabulary, fluency, grammar, listening, reading, writing, or all of those?"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Okay. I made a new friend, but they hardly speak English. I'd like to help her learn. It would be outside of the classroom, at least for now."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It might help if you told me the goal you had for your target language.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'To get to a good level of conversational English'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Great!  Do you want to understand written and spoken English well, and do you want to be able to do all of these things for yourself, or would it be fine for your friend to always have an interpreter for her?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Mainly spoken English. An interpreter could help, but I'd like to help her understand the basics of spoken English."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Got it.  Do you have any particular goals for this process?   Will you have a written curriculum, or are you just going to work on whatever your friend is interested in learning?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "We'd like to make a loose plan based on her interests."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'That makes sense!   Do you know if she already has an interest in learning English?  What are her goals?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'She does. She wants to be able to introduce herself and tell people about her interests. She wants to learn the ways of asking, thanking, greeting, for example, to begin with.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'What is your role in this process?   Are you both going to be in class together?   Are you going to do it together with her?  Do you have plans for how this will happen?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'The plan is for me to be her unofficial teacher. To start with. Maybe later she can take lessons by herself.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I think it\'s a good idea to have a schedule and curriculum with concrete goals.  When I read about "disengagement" in second language learning, I see many teachers and scholars recommending that the students and the teacher plan together on a daily schedule.  What do you think about that idea?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay. Yes, but I\'m unsure what you mean by "disengagement".'}]
