DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you tell me the basics of travel insurance?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sure! Here’s a list of things I can tell you:  \n1.    You can purchase travel insurance to protect yourself against financial loss in case you’re a victim of a disaster (this is called a ‘disaster policy’), which can include situations like flight delays, cancellations, robbery, lost luggage, and theft of valuables or cash.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you expand more on your first point?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Sure. I can tell you the importance of travel insurance, and how you might want to think about it. I can also explain how much insurance costs, and what plans you might be eligible for.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Well, I wanted to you tell me more about a disaster policy.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'A disaster policy usually pays for losses that you incur because of an unexpected disaster, like a hurricane, wildfire, or the 2008 earthquake in China. You may find that a travel insurance company offers coverage for several different kinds of disasters, like fire, flood, theft, hurricane, earthquake, terrorism, and accident.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is there any disaster you can think of that they would not cover? I mean, they pretty much cover all disasters, it seems'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I'd like to expand my knowledge of poetry, are there some books you can recommend?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'What do you mean by “poetry”, is it poems with meter, or poems which are really short? What type of poems do you like? What’s the kind of poetry you don’t like?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I like lyric poetry. Shorter is better. I don't like poems that are too complex or dense."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Do you like a strong sense of melody, or free verse?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Free verse, mostly.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Have you read poetry by any of these poets before?  I'll read some of the poems from each of their collections and see if any of them appeals to you.  This poem is by Adrienne Rich, and is from her volume The Dream of a Common Language.  Do you like it?  Here's one by Mary Oliver, and one by Audre Lorde, from her book New and Selected Poems.  Would you like to hear the last one, by Naomi Shihab Nye?"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'There are some good recommendations. I will try some. Are they all writing free verse poetry?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes.  Are you interested in some examples of free verse poetry by different poets?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Yes, could you mention a few more living poets who are writing free verse poems?'}]
