DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do you know if you are entering menopause?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You’re talking about the time in a woman’s life when her menstrual periods are much less frequent, and sometimes the periods stop completely. Menopause is defined as the time when a woman has gone 12 months without menstruating, and it’s usually reached around the age of 50.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you enter menopause at an earlier age?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It is technically possible to enter menopause before the age of 50, although it’s quite rare. Some women will experience a reduction in their periods, and menopause can begin a few years before this, so the average age of menopause is usually stated as the age when the periods stop.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What are other symptoms of menopause?'}]
