DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "My bearded dragon isn't eating his greens. What can I do to make it more appealing?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Can I give you some guidance on selecting greens for your bearded dragon?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Yes please. Which greens are more appealing to bearded dragons?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'There are many different kinds of greens that bearded dragons will eat, but in general the best greens are small leaves from dark green plants, like alfalfa, and broadleaf vegetables like kale and collard greens.  Since bearded dragons are diurnal, they will generally be more active during the day, so they are often most active at about midday.  When choosing greens, you want to pick those that are healthy and intact, rather than damaged or wilted.  They are best if they are small enough to be eaten whole.  Also, bearded dragons have teeth that are quite sharp, so it’s important that they eat from a quiet area, such as their enclosure.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Thank you that is very helpful. What other greens can I give them?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'In general, a good variety of greens is best, as bearded dragons can benefit from both calcium and fiber.  I can offer more specific advice if you give me the name of your specific bearded dragon.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'central bearded dragon'}]
