apart, and pointing forward.  When you stand up straight and extend your arm, a right-hand punching posture is commonly used.  This means you’re pointing your fist forward and your elbow is close to your side.  Your back is straight and your chest is up.  Second, your chin should be tucked in to your neck.  This increases the power in your punch and can help prevent you from getting hurt.  Third, your fist should be loosely closed, with your fingers relaxed.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I will keep this in mind when practicing on a punching bag.'}]
