DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Every time I want to use gravy, I find myself putting it on mashed potatoes. Are there any other recipes one can use gravy for?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Yes, you can use gravy on cooked pasta and rice. It makes them taste a bit like creamy rice pudding. It's also nice over apple pie.  If you're doing something fancier, like a stir-fry or something, then I would suggest using gravy to baste your food, then finish it off with a drizzle of soy sauce or some other sweet-salty sauce on top."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'This is all very new to me. Gravy over rice sounds like it could be good'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Gravy over rice is actually a very traditional southern-style dish. Rice is the starch you use to absorb the gravy, and give it the extra creaminess, but if you use white rice the texture will be a little dry.  If you use instant rice it will be perfect.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I'm gonna try it out. Sounds like it could be delicious. Some steak, rice and gravy?"}]
