DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I want to donate to a charity, but know that lots of charities don't use the money properly. Which charities are most efficient?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "That's a great question, and the answer is quite complicated.  Perhaps it would be easier to first make a few assumptions about what a “most efficient” charity would be like, and then evaluate what types of charities share those characteristics.  One easy way to start thinking about what qualities of a charity make it efficient would be to think about its administrative overhead.  Administrative overhead is the expense of doing business, which includes staff salaries, facilities expenses, other expenses related to the running of the business, etc.  A charity with low administrative overhead will have a lower cost per dollar raised, so it can have a larger impact for a given dollar donated.  On the other hand, a charity with high administrative overhead may be able to raise more money through their business activities, but those funds won’t translate to better services.  If we think about efficiency this way, then there’s actually a very large number of charities that could be considered “efficient”, even if they might not be doing the most good overall.  An example of a non-charity would be an employee-owned business, which would be quite efficient, but there’s nothing else like it."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I see. So where does the money go with charities that have high administrative costs? Does it go to advertising or something?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Some of it goes to advertising, but advertising is generally considered a necessary overhead in order to fundraise.  However, charities should probably invest at least some of their funds into their day-to-day operations.  There are also often funds that are set aside for short term projects, but have little long-term benefits for the charity.  In general, it’s difficult to measure how much of a charity’s funding is being spent on overhead, so we would need to be specific about which charities we’re talking about.  There are many charities who do a great job of spending a large portion of their funds on their programs, while also being quite efficient at running their business.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Do you know which charities have the least admistrative costs?'}]
