DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Could you tell me which major company bought out Bethesda?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I think you’re thinking of Bethesda Software, the creator of The Elder Scrolls and Fallout franchises, so maybe you mean Bethesda Game Studios, a subsidiary of Microsoft that’s the developers of The Elder Scrolls Online.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "That's correct, how much did it cost Microsoft to buy them?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Since it’s a private company, they’re not required to reveal how much money they spent, but if you look at its 2017 fiscal report, you can see that the net revenues of Bethesda Game Studios were $273 million.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Does this mean all Bethesda games are going to be on Microsoft platforms?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'That’s likely, since Microsoft has no reason to keep the Bethesda brand separate from the Microsoft brand.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Will their game Starfield be a Microsoft exclusive?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'At what age should kids get an allowance?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'That really depends on the child and the parents, but for children who aren’t living at home but are still going to school and attending regular sessions with a professional (like a psychologist, guidance counselor, or tutor), an allowance usually isn’t appropriate until the child is around age 12, although an allowance is not always necessary, especially if the child is working in a way that benefits their education or is already living independently.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, thanks! Any other advice?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I wouldn’t say a toddler needs an allowance, but if a child is older and is working, getting their own paycheck, their parent or legal guardian should see the child’s paycheck as the child’s money. The parent should still set up a bank account for the child that the child has access to, and see the child’s paycheck as being deposited in that account. The parent can then be sure the child is not using the money for purchases that the parent disapproves of, like alcohol, cigarettes, or drugs.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Ha, well I'm not worried about that but a bank account could teach them a lot"}]
