DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I cite my sources in an essay?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You could just explain in the essay that all of the ideas came from somewhere else, like a book or an article or a speech. You could make it a part of the essay that it was based on these sources, so the reader knows where it came from, and isn’t misled that the ideas are your own.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is there a specific format I need to follow?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Your essay should probably be written as though it were a regular book, with an “Author”, a “Title”, a “Publisher”, and a “Date”, and probably “Annotated Bibliography” at the end. \nAfter that, the citation needs to tell where you got the material from, and it should tell how to get to it.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Ok thank you. That's helpful."}]
