DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What can I do to raise my credit score?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'You should start by tracking and keeping an eye on your credit report.  Pay your bills on time.  You can also apply for a secured credit card with a low limit so you can rebuild your credit after a debt problem.  If you can’t do that, the second-best thing is to find and apply for a secured loan.  That’s a loan that you pay with money from your savings account rather than paying it with a credit card, and you can set the loan rate based on how good your credit is.  Then the loan will pay itself off quickly and you can re-establish your credit score.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Anything else?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Other than a secured loan, the best option is to pay off your debts so that your monthly payments are very small and your credit score can rise.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Thanks'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What can I say in a tribute to someone that died.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Tributes can be powerful things, and the ones I’ve seen most often are about life, and the passing of time.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you help me write one please?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'If you’re struggling to find words, you could start by writing about how you’re feeling, or how you think others will be feeling.  Then perhaps you could pick a few ways that the person will be remembered, or a special characteristic that she had.  For example, you could describe her kindness, or her love of animals, or her dedication to public service.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'That is a good start. Thank you.'}]
