DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "Every now and then I hear about the 'Iran Contra' thing but I don't really know what it is. Can you summarize?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The Iran Contra scandal was a series of illegal activities conducted by the Reagan Administration between 1984 and 1987.  One aspect of this involved illegally selling arms to Iran, which were then sold to the Contras in Nicaragua.  In another, the CIA illegally sold weapons to the Contras as well.  A total of over half a million dollars in profits from the sales of these weapons was then illegally diverted to the Contras.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Why were those things illegal if the government was the one doing them?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Both were.  Selling weapons to Iran was illegal, and this violated the existing U.S. law prohibiting aid to governments that are officially recognized as enemies, as well as violating the Iran arms embargo.  The CIA’s actions were also illegal, and violated the Reagan administration’s policy not to provide weapons to groups classified as terrorist organizations.  The Reagan administration was also well-known for sometimes bending the law in some ways, in an effort to accomplish its goals.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What was the goal of all this?'}]
