DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'I am in the mood for Chinese food, but takeout is too expensive. What are some Chinese-inspired meals I can make at home?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'If you can, buy the meat and vegetables in bulk at your local supermarket or grocer, and freeze them for a month. Then when you need Chinese food you can pull out some frozen meat and vegetables to make one of these classic Chinese dishes.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'That sounds good. What Chinese dishes can I make?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Great question! I’ll give you a short introduction to four popular Chinese cuisines.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, great. Please do.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'In Chinese-American cuisine you will see dishes like General Tso’s chicken, egg foo young, hot and sour soup, lo mein noodles and fortune cookies.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Great. Egg foo young sounds good. What is in that?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Why does my skin get more dry in cold weather?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Skin becomes drier and more vulnerable to damage when the air is drier. Since cold weather means that there’s less moisture in the air, our skin loses moisture more rapidly. It’s a protective measure so that our skin can adjust, but it’s really important to moisturize our skin and be careful when going outside, especially when the sun is very strong.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How can I better protect my skin from breakouts in the cold?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'As I’m sure you know, the best way to avoid breakouts is to keep your skin clean and avoid touching your face. You should wash your hands often and use moisturizers and creams to keep your skin hydrated. A pimple is the result of a pore getting clogged, so you can try gentle face exfoliation with a soft washcloth.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How often should I be exfoliating?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It’s fine to exfoliate once every week or two, though sometimes you can feel like you’re overdoing it. You should only exfoliate if your skin seems dry, and it’s a good idea to only exfoliate in the morning, since that’s when skin is at its most hydrated and healthy.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What kinds of exfoliants are good for your face?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'A light chemical exfoliant is a good way to naturally clean your skin and is gentler than physical exfoliants like face brushes. An example of a chemical exfoliant is glycolic acid, which is derived from fruit acid. Another great natural exfoliant is sour milk, and you can buy that from a cosmetics store. Gentle physical exfoliants like face brushes are fine for the occasional treat, but don’t use them too often.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Do you have any brands you can recommend to me?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is there a way that you can get your pets to shed less fur all over the house?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I’m not really a pet, and I don’t have pets. But if I had pets, I might try a few strategies. Like putting them in their carriers before shaving, or putting their carrier by the bath tub, so they’re already in a “shaved” state when you wash them.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I never thought of shaving them. I wonder if there is an attachment for my vacuum to suck the hair right off the dog?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you explain what rabies is?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Rhabdomyolysis is a muscle-wasting disease, usually caused by a brain infection, such as encephalitis. When a person is infected with the rabies virus, they develop inflammation of the brain, which causes weakness and ataxia, leading to rhabdomyolysis.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How is rabies spread?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'In people, the rabies virus is usually spread by bites from infected animals (canines). Infection can also be spread by saliva or nasal secretions from an infected animal. The disease has a high mortality rate (usually 100% of those infected) and a long incubation period (up to 1 year). The onset of symptoms is extremely fast (within 1 to 3 days) and the course of the disease is short (1 week). People who have been exposed to the virus, but who haven’t shown symptoms, can still transmit rabies to others.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Why is rabies so fatal?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Many animals have a strong immune response to the rabies virus, allowing them to recover. In humans, however, the virus uses the body’s immune response to spread through the brain. It damages the brain and spinal cord, causing inflammation that damages the tissue and causes symptoms like fever, headache, and vomiting. As the virus attacks the brain and spinal cord, it damages the brain cells’ ability to function, which makes the infected person unable to breathe on their own and ultimately die.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What are symptoms of rabies?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'How do I make a Christmas garland?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Using craft foam and a glue gun and a hot glue gun. The foam will look good and thick enough for Christmas decorations, you can choose between a bunch of different designs.  For the glue gun, I’d suggest getting a small, kid-sized one, unless you have a big tree to decorate.  And for the hot glue gun, you’ll need one with a big glue head, so it doesn’t get clogged up or run out of glue.  You can get these at Home Depot or Lowes or some big box store.  After you get everything, it should only take a few minutes to make a garland.  Then you can hang it around the Christmas tree with colored ribbon or string.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Any other ideas?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, you can also make a Christmas tree crown using glitter and star stickers.  You could do something simple like this and buy some ornaments or Christmas lights and put them on the crown.  I could help you make a crown like this if you want me to, I know how to sew.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I was still asking for garland ideas'}]
