DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you help me to understand what stoicism is?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Yes, I think I can! First of all, it’s a philosophy, but it can be applied to almost everything in life. The best definition of stoicism I know is in the book How To Win Friends And Influence People by Dale Carnegie. This book also explains that stoicism is all about controlling your emotions, not letting other people control your emotions, and that it’s also related to positive thinking.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'When did stoicism first show up?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The first written record of stoicism is found in the book Discourses of Epictetus. That was written in approximately 100 A.D. Also, many people are interested in philosophy because of the Stoic philosopher Epictetus, who lived in Greece around 50-120 A.D.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Who are some followers of stoicism?'}]
