DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'I want to quit smoking. What are some methods I can use?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Hm, to be honest, most “quit smoking” advice you get from people around you is probably not very helpful, since most people don’t have any idea what is effective, or what it’s actually like to quit smoking, so they might be biased and might not have any real data to back up what they’re saying.  The current state of the art seems to be for you to quit gradually, by reducing the number of cigarettes you smoke, and then to continue to reduce the number of cigarettes for a while until you’re smoking 0 cigarettes a day.  It’s also good to change up your smoking routine: don’t have a fixed location or fixed time you smoke, and it might also help to switch to electronic cigarettes.  And also talk to a doctor about what might help for you specifically, they’re likely to have more info that’s useful to you.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Great ideas! What should I do if I slip up?'}]
