DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "What's the best career path for someone with the INFP personality type?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The INFP personality type is one that will probably fit well in the health field, since it’s somewhat of a dual type. INFPs have relatively well-developed intuitions and are prone to sympathy, but have a somewhat weak sense of self, since they’re very driven by their emotions.  I’d also recommend going into therapy.  After all, an INFP’s most well-developed attribute is their emotional empathy, and that can be used to help others.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, so therapy, or counselling could be a good option?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'If you wanted to pursue that, yes.  There are many different kinds of therapy, and as an INFP, I think you could also consider doing a type of creative expression, like writing or painting.   But if you’re worried about practical questions, remember that there are all sorts of types of jobs that are related to counseling or therapy.  You could also consider medicine, since INFPs are so well-versed in empathy and also other emotional attributes.  Do you have other questions, or should we discuss any other careers?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay. Well, I am also interested in creative expression.'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I recently learned that I'm diabetic, but I'm really nervous around needles. Is there a way for me to take care of my diabetes with insulin without using needles and shots?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "If you're talking about insulin as a way to manage diabetes, your best option is definitely injections of insulin through the skin.  That's because the injection won't affect your blood sugar, but the glucose in your bloodstream will be slowly absorbed by your tissues and over time it should lower your blood sugar level back to normal.  A high blood sugar level can have many effects, and it's much more dangerous to try to deal with it through something you eat."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Are there any alternative methods of getting insulin that don't involve needles?"}]
