t sleeping, like thinking they’re not good enough, or that they’ll never get enough sleep.\n   - CBT-I helps you recognize and change these negative thoughts. For example, if you think, “I’ll never be able to sleep,” the therapist might help you reframe that thought into something like, “I can improve my sleep habits", "</think>\n\nThe best time to plant **spinach** in **Maryland** is **late spring to early summer**, specifically **late April to early June**, depending on the local climate and the specific variety of spinach you're planting. Here's a breakdown to help you determine the optimal planting window:\n\n---\n\n### **1. General Planting Window**\n- **Best time**: **April to June** (depending on the variety and climate).\n- **Avoid planting in late May to early June**, as this may not be ideal for all varieties, especially those that are more heat-tolerant.\n\n---\n\n### **2. Factors to Consider**\n- **Climate**: Maryland has four seasons, and the growing season is relatively short.\n- **Soil type and condition**: Spinach prefers well-drained, fertile soil with a slightly acidic pH (6.0–7.0).\n- **Soil preparation**: Ensure the area is prepared before planting (till and amend with organic matter or compost).\n", "What can I do with Halloween candy I don't want?\n\nHi, I was just wondering what I can do with the Halloween candy that I don't want. I know I can use it to make a candy bar, but that's not the only thing I can do. I also know I can make a spooky decoration. But there are so many other things. I don't want to waste it, so I'd like to find out what else I can do with it. Maybe even some ideas that are not so obvious.\n\nOkay, I need to think of other ideas. Let me see, the candy is already going to be wasted, but I want to use it in a unique way. Maybe I can make a Halloween mask, but that seems too obvious. I want to think of something more creative. Maybe I can make a small craft, like a Halloween decoration for my room, but that's what I already 