DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "Hey! I'm struggling to learn how to meal prep. What are some staples that I can make as a beginner?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I can definitely help with that. First of all, do you have a slow cooker?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'I have a slow cooker and I love it! So far I only know how to make pulled chicken in it'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Great. There are tons of slow cooker recipes available online, so it's really easy to start cooking and to vary up your diet. A lot of people like to put a slow cooker with some stew meat and vegetables on before they go to work, so they get a hot meal that is already cooked at dinnertime. Slow cookers also make it easy to do bacon-wrapped filet mignon, pork chops, brisket, pulled chicken, and many other popular meats."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Wow! That sounds awesome! Are there any sides of snacks or should also be including in my meal prep?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I can definitely help with that. I really like to make chopped broccoli, cauliflower, and sweet potatoes into mash potatoes. So in the crock pot, you just chop all the veggies up, add in a touch of olive oil, and some chicken or beef broth or vegetable broth, and cook it. Then you throw in a box of pre-made potato packets.  You just heat it up and you have home-made mashed potatoes, and your family will love it! It’s a super simple way to introduce new foods into your diet.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Sounds like a great side dish! I'm going to try this after my next grocery trip for sure!"}]
