DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Which wearable tracker is the cheapest?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It seems to me that if you’re not looking for something very basic, the cheapest tracker is usually the one you actually end up using. So one way to think about it is how you’ll be using it, and what features matter to you, and then try to find a tracker that has those features. For example, you might only care about location accuracy, rather than battery life or compatibility with more than one brand of watch, so you could look for the cheapest watches that have all of those features. Or you could look for a price range in mind and see what your options are.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is the average price of a Fitbit?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Not sure, I’ve never used one. I can check: they’re about $100 right now.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Does a fitbit come with a warranty?'}]
