DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is Oktoberfest?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Oktoberfest is an annual event held in Munich, Germany.  It’s a very large festival that takes place over a few weeks every year.  It’s mainly a beer festival, but people also eat lots of traditional food and drink a lot of traditional drinks like beer, wine, schnapps, and cider.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'That sounds like fun. What traditional foods are served?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Some traditional foods include, pretzels, bratwurst, sausages, roasted chicken, roasted potatoes, cabbage, and sauerkraut.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What kind of beer is most popular at German Oktoberfests?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The German lagers Oktoberfestbier and Märzenbier are the most popular.  Those beers are actually brewed during the year, and are aged, so they taste better in the winter.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How could I hold my own Oktoberfest celebration?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'I like to host guests at my home from time to time, and I am gathering  recipes of different dishes and drinks to keep things interesting. I am interested in trying some South African  dishes. Can you give me a recipe for Biltong?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Great, I can help with that.  Biltong is a sort of dry meat similar to a sausage. The most common kind is made from beef or game meat, but many other kinds of game meat are possible, including ostrich and antelope.  It’s typically braised for an hour or two, to make it more tender.  It can also be dried or grilled, and then eaten as is.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "So it is essentially South Africa's take on jerky."}]
