DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Where should I shop for a good motorcycle helmet?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Great question! I suggest starting at SuperSales.com, as this is a reputable and established website that has been around for many years.  I’d also suggest checking out what people are saying online, and if you’re local, you might also try shopping locally at a store you’ve used before, since you can get a sense of the level of service that they provide and whether they care about customers’ needs. \nOne more thing you might also want to check is if your local motorcycle store has a helmets, like they do here in New York City.  I have some knowledge of a few New York City stores, like one that has a self-service section and one that has test riding to help you try the helmet on before you buy it, and I’d recommend shopping at the one that offers self-service, as it is easier to browse in and you don’t need to wait in line to test ride.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Great advice but I’m Atlanta and not in New York!'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I've heard a lot about RSS feeds but I have no idea what they are. Can you explain them to me?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Sure! RSS (Really Simple Syndication) is a technology that enables the dissemination of new content in a way that is easy for both consumers and producers of the content.  You can think of it as a standardized way for websites to send each other updates, much like how your email inbox works, except that the content is in a format that you're more likely to want to read (like web pages)."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Specifically, I've heard about people using RSS feeds to download their favorite podcasts when the apps themselves don't allow you to download, only stream. How do RSS feeds do this?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Ah, sure! When a podcast uses RSS, it publishes its feeds on its website and sends them to a central server.  This allows the feeds to be accessed by anyone, and so this is essentially a way to make the podcast available to anyone who wants to.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Is there a way to search for individual RSS feeds? Can I just use google, or do I need another search engine?'}]
