DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What are some etiquette culture tips that you know of when traveling to Japan?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It depends on how much you know about Japanese etiquette.  If you don’t have much knowledge, my first tip would be to just not be weird or un-Japanese.  It can be hard to balance, but that’s the basic goal!  A few other tips could be to always smile, and speak politely.  You’ll also want to stay on your best behavior at all times, as in how you behave in public or with strangers.  What kind of trip are you going on?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Fun trip. Those are very general tips, and for all I know, they don't even care about smiling. Not everyone cares about smiles. Do you have any other tips?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'For a trip to Japan, I would say you should probably try to speak Japanese, and avoid speaking English as much as possible.  That’s not too uncommon though, because some tourists are still curious about learning Japanese.  I can show you some relevant terms that might be useful for you on a trip to Japan.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Okay, sure, learn some Japanese. What other tips do you have, if any?'}]
