DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I'm thinking of getting a cat. What should I know beforehand?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I think you would benefit from knowing that a cat is capable of making an indelible impression on your life.  It is likely to spend significant time roaming freely in your home, and you may need to ensure that you have appropriate cat food and cat litter, which can become stinky and unpleasant as the cat learns to use the litter box.  But you can do this!  Cats can be a joy, especially if you are an animal lover.  A good rule of thumb is to not over-indulge your cat, but instead allow the cat to wander freely, with lots of mental stimulation, both inside the house and outside.  You could also try watching cat videos on Youtube, and seeing what seems to interest your cat.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'That sounds like good advice. I want to adopt one from a shelter. Should I get a kitten or an older cat?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Generally, adopting an older cat that has already been house-trained is the easiest way to go, but you can adopt a kitten from a shelter or buy a kitten from a breeder and train it for a year or so until it becomes house-trained.  What is your tolerance for household messes?  Do you have a family or roommate?  Do you have a busy lifestyle, or do you work at home?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'You should always advise people to adopt from a shelter or rescue. I have a high tolerance for mess. I have a boyfriend, but he likes animals. I work from home.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Great!  We have similar preferences here.  It’s a good idea to be open-minded about kittens, but to spend some time trying to understand the temperaments of the cats you are considering, in order to pick one that will likely fit into your lifestyle.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'What kinds of supplies do I need to bring my new cat home?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Who were The Five Nations? I know one was Mohawk but what about the other four?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'So the Iroquois Confederacy was composed of five different nations: the Mohawk, Oneida, Onondaga, Cayuga, and Seneca.  Each nation had its own chief and legislature, and they held council meetings together.  This gave them a lot of power against European settlers, and sometimes allowed them to join together as a unified force.  It was particularly useful when defending their territory from European expansion.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Where are they now?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'They were organized as a confederacy between the years 1614 and 1768.  Then they decided to split into individual nations, and today they’re spread throughout the U.S.  Several are in the middle of New York state, one is in Ohio, and others are in the mid-west.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Was the Seneca tribe named after the Roam Seneca or is that just a coincidence?'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'These days, many times, people like to animate videos of TED talks, or speeches. Why is animating speeches such a popular theme these days?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'A couple of hypotheses come to mind:  First, videos of speeches are very easy to work with.  One thing you could do is make a timeline showing key moments in the video, with different illustrations for each key moment, to give a sense of the speaker’s feelings.  But also, animated videos give people the sense that you’re exploring the ideas in the speech even more deeply, and that you’re able to make associations that were maybe not even in the speaker’s mind.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Can you give me an example of that?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'This example is one that I’ve had recently in mind, which I think shows a particularly creative use of speech animation.  In the video “How to Control Your Emotions”, Ken Robinson, a well-known author on creativity, explains why his culture is losing the capacity to innovate.  He looks forward into the future and suggests a question that’s still unanswered: how will children be educated to develop their own creative abilities?  In the video, Robinson uses a theme from the poem “The Road Not Taken” by Robert Frost as a conceptual jumping off point.  \nSo imagine the future society, where Robinson’s line of thinking has gained currency, and children are encouraged to make some real changes in their learning.  I'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Thank you for further information, although that was too much information. Can you give me the gist in two or three sentences?'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'That would be great.  Let me try it again.  I think that animated videos of speeches are interesting because they create a visual impression of the speaker’s ideas and emotions.  With animation, it’s possible to explore the ideas in the speech much more deeply and you can give a sense of the speaker’s feelings even when those feelings weren’t part of the original message.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'That makes more sense. I suppose you can also accentuate or emphasized points that were more subtle. Originally'}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': "I'm trying to figure out how to best train an AI assistant. How should I go about doing that?"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Are you just talking about how to train an existing AI assistant or actually building a new one from scratch?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I'm looking to train an existing AI, like you."}]
DIALOGUE PAIRS: [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Which nut is one of the healthier ones, to snack on? Cashews taste great, but others might be better.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'My research says a nut is nutritious if it is high in fat and high in calories.  Cashews contain more fat than most other nuts, and are also high in calories, so they are very nutritious.  Walnuts and almonds are also high in fat, and a “handful” of them is also a small caloric amount, so they too are healthy.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "I've heard almonds are a healthier choice for blood sugar support, than others. And peanuts seem good at times."}]
