iate with riding and farming.\n\n### 2. **Why Are Zebras Different?**\n   - **Appearance**: Zebras are **not** "funny looking" in the way that many people perceive typical horses. They have **distinctive markings**—black and white stripes—on their coat.\n   - **Physical Traits**: \n     - Zebras are **larger** than most horses.\n     - They have **smaller hooves**.\n     -', '</think>\n\nThat’s great to hear! It’s really rewarding to know your dog is happy and close to you. Dogs can be quite expressive, and when they show you that they like to be near you, it’s a sign that they’re feeling loved and secure. Just make sure to give them a cozy bed, maybe some favorite blankets, and some gentle attention when they’re asleep. They’ll appreciate the little things, and it’ll make your time together even more special. 😊', "</think>\n\nThat’s a great question! So, you're interested in **minerals that are nearly as hard as diamond**, which is **10 on the Mohs scale** (the hardest known mineral).\n\n### **Diamond** is the hardest known mineral, with a **Mohs hardness of 10**.\n\n### **Minerals that are nearly as hard as diamond** (i.e., **9 or higher** on the Mohs scale):\n\n1. **Corundum**  \n   - **Hardness:** 8 (very hard, very resistant to scratching)\n   - **Common minerals:**\n     - **Ruby** (a type of corundum)\n     - **Sapphire** (another type of corundum)\n   - **Uses:** Jewelers' stones, industrial abrasives\n\n2. **Corundum (Corundum, Rubies, Sapphires)**  \n   - **Hardness:** 8\n   - **Examples:** Rubies"]
